ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231030T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=gh
 liu@gatech.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:ghliu@gatech.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ti
 anrong.chen@gatech.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:tianrong.chen@gatech.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20231030T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Guan-Horn
 g Liu once again :)<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Mirror Diffusion Models for 
 Constrained and Watermarked Generation </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2
 310.01236">https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.01236</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Liu\,+G">Guan-Horng Liu</a>\, <a 
 href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Chen\,+T">
 Tianrong Chen</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=autho
 r&amp\;query=Theodorou\,+E+A">Evangelos A. Theodorou</a>\, <a href="https:/
 /arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Tao\,+M">Molei Tao</a>)
 <br>Modern successes of diffusion models in learning complex\, high-dimensi
 onal data distributions are attributed\, in part\, to their capability to c
 onstruct diffusion processes with analytic transition kernels and score fun
 ctions. The tractability results in a simulation-free framework with stable
  regression losses\, from which reversed\, generative processes can be lear
 ned at scale. However\, when data is confined to a constrained set as oppos
 ed to a standard Euclidean space\, these desirable characteristics appear t
 o be lost based on prior attempts. In this work\, we propose Mirror Diffusi
 on Models (MDM)\, a new class of diffusion models that generate data on con
 vex constrained sets without losing any tractability. This is achieved by l
 earning diffusion processes in a dual space constructed from a mirror map\,
  which\, crucially\, is a standard Euclidean space. We derive efficient com
 putation of mirror maps for popular constrained sets\, such as simplices an
 d ℓ2-balls\, showing significantly improved performance of MDM over existin
 g methods. For safety and privacy purposes\, we also explore constrained se
 ts as a new mechanism to embed invisible but quantitative information (i.e.
 \, watermarks) in generated data\, for which MDM serves as a compelling app
 roach. Our work brings new algorithmic opportunities for learning tractable
  diffusion on complex domains.<br><b> <br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i
 >Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.  </
 i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5
 pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a
 ><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href
 ="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0
 uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc
 85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\,
  recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.
 com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></
 u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250330T034726Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
