DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240318T160000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240318T170000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=om
 er.bar-tal@weizmann.ac.il;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:omer.bar-tal@weizmann.ac.il
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240318T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Omer Bar-
 Tal from Weizmann institute.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>MultiDiffusion: Fus
 ing Diffusion Paths for Controlled Image Generation </b><a href="https://ar
 xiv.org/abs/2302.08113">https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.08113</a> (<a href="http
 s://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bar-Tal\,+O">Omer Bar-
 Tal</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query
 =Yariv\,+L">Lior Yariv</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtyp
 e=author&amp\;query=Lipman\,+Y">Yaron Lipman</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.o
 rg/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Dekel\,+T">Tali Dekel</a>)<br>Rec
 ent advances in text-to-image generation with diffusion models present tran
 sformative capabilities in image quality. However\, user controllability of
  the generated image\, and fast adaptation to new tasks still remains an op
 en challenge\, currently mostly addressed by costly and long re-training an
 d fine-tuning or ad-hoc adaptations to specific image generation tasks. In 
 this work\, we present MultiDiffusion\, a unified framework that enables ve
 rsatile and controllable image generation\, using a pre-trained text-to-ima
 ge diffusion model\, without any further training or finetuning. At the cen
 ter of our approach is a new generation process\, based on an optimization 
 task that binds together multiple diffusion generation processes with a sha
 red set of parameters or constraints. We show that MultiDiffusion can be re
 adily applied to generate high quality and diverse images that adhere to us
 er-provided controls\, such as desired aspect ratio (e.g.\, panorama)\, and
  spatial guiding signals\, ranging from tight segmentation masks to boundin
 g boxes. Project webpage: this https URL<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<
 br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am 
 PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4
 vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5
 pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b
 ><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31g
 c85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-
 FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming 
 papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hanne
 s-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-gro
 up</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
