ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob_R20250630T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=se
 rgey.pozdnyakov@epfl.ch;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:sergey.pozdnyakov@epfl.ch
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20251020T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Sergey Po
 zdnyakov who is a PostDoc at EPFL<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Lookup multiva
 riate Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.07
 103">https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.07103</a><b> (</b><a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Pozdnyakov\,+S">Sergey Pozdnyakov<
 /a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Sch
 waller\,+P">Philippe Schwaller</a>)<br>High-dimensional linear mappings\, o
 r linear layers\, dominate both the parameter count and the computational c
 ost of most modern deep-learning models. We introduce a general drop-in rep
 lacement\, lookup multivariate Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks (lmKANs)\, which 
 deliver a substantially better trade-off between capacity and inference cos
 t. Our construction expresses a general high-dimensional mapping through tr
 ainable low-dimensional multivariate functions. These functions can carry d
 ozens or hundreds of trainable parameters each\, and yet it takes only a fe
 w multiplications to compute them because they are implemented as spline lo
 okup tables. Empirically\, lmKANs reduce inference FLOPs by up to 6.0x whil
 e matching the flexibility of MLPs in general high-dimensional function app
 roximation. In another feedforward fully connected benchmark\, on the tabul
 ar-like dataset of randomly displaced methane configurations\, lmKANs enabl
 e more than 10x higher H100 throughput at equal accuracy. Within frameworks
  of Convolutional Neural Networks\, lmKAN-based CNNs cut inference FLOPs at
  matched accuracy by 1.6-2.1x and by 1.7x on the CIFAR-10 and ImageNet-1k d
 atasets\, respectively. Our code\, including dedicated CUDA kernels\, is av
 ailable online at <a href="https://github.com/schwallergroup/lmkan">this ht
 tps URL</a>.<br><b><br></b><br><b><br></b><br><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i
 >Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i><br><a href
 ="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target
 ="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
 </a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a h
 ref="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkh
 O7WlRsyElg" target="_blank"><u>https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite
 /zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg</u></a><br><br><b>All information: Sch
 edule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><a href
 ="https://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking" target="_blank">https://p
 ortal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking</a><b></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u
 ><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T170220Z
