BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220308T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220308T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20220118T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=chaitj
 o@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:chaitjo@gmail.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220308T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="htt
 ps://www.chaitjo.com/" id="ow531" __is_owner="true">Chaitanya K. Joshi </a>
 is an incoming PhD student at the University of Cambridge\, supervised by P
 rof. Pietro Liò. His research explores the intersection of Graph and Geomet
 ric Deep Learning with applications in biomedicine and drug discovery. He p
 reviously worked on Graph Neural Network architectures and applications in 
 Combinatorial Optimization at the NTU Graph Deep Learning Lab and A*STAR\, 
 Singapore.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Recent Advances in Deep Learning for 
 Routing Problems</b> <a href="https://www.chaitjo.com/post/deep-learning-fo
 r-routing-problems" id="ow527" __is_owner="true">https://www.chaitjo.com/po
 st/deep-learning-for-routing-problems</a> (Chaitanya K. Joshi\, Rishabh Ana
 nd) 2022<br>Developing Graph Neural Network-driven solvers for combinatoria
 l optimization problems such as the Travelling Salesperson Problem have see
 n a surge of academic interest recently. This talk aims to serve as a whirl
 wind tour of this research area. We first presents a&nbsp\;Neural Combinato
 rial Optimization&nbsp\;pipeline that unifies several recently proposed mod
 els into one single framework. Through the lens of the pipeline\, we analyz
 e recent advances in deep learning for routing problems and provide new dir
 ections to stimulate future research.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br>
 </b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PT</i><br><a hre
 f="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https
 ://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>
 Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://jo
 in.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">http
 s://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>z
 Elmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming p
 apers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes
 -stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-grou
 p</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195612Z
