DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220614T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220614T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=karoli
 s.mart@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:karolis.mart@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=loukas
 an@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:loukasan@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=mk
 arolis@ethz.ch;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:mkarolis@ethz.ch
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220614T170000
CREATED:20220820T195614Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="https://di
 sco.ethz.ch/members/mkarolis" id="ow561" __is_owner="true">Karolis Martinku
 s</a>&nbsp\;and Dr&nbsp\;<a href="https://andreasloukas.blog/" id="ow571" _
 _is_owner="true">Andreas Loukas</a>. Karolis is a PhD student at ETH Zurich
  working with Prof. Roger Wattenhofer. He has a lot of work on graph genera
 tion and GNNs in general.&nbsp\;</html-blob><br><html-blob>Andreas received
  his PhD from TU Delft and did PostDocs at TU Berlin and EPFL before starti
 ng as Principal Scientist at Genentech.&nbsp\;</html-blob><br><html-blob><b
 r><b>Paper:</b><br>SPECTRE : Spectral Conditioning Helps to Overcome the Ex
 pressivity Limits of One-shot Graph Generators&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv
 .org/abs/2204.01613">https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.01613</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="h
 ttps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Martinkus%2C+K"><u>
 Karolis Martinkus</u></a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?sear
 chtype=author&amp\;query=Loukas%2C+A">Andreas Loukas</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="h
 ttps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Perraudin%2C+N">Nat
 hanaël Perraudin</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtyp
 e=author&amp\;query=Wattenhofer%2C+R" id="ow600" __is_owner="true">Roger Wa
 ttenhofer</a>)<br>We approach the graph generation problem from a spectral 
 perspective by first generating the dominant parts of the graph Laplacian s
 pectrum and then building a graph matching these eigenvalues and eigenvecto
 rs. Spectral conditioning allows for direct modeling of the global and loca
 l graph structure and helps to overcome the expressivity and mode collapse 
 issues of one-shot graph generators. Our novel GAN\, called SPECTRE\, enabl
 es the one-shot generation of much larger graphs than previously possible w
 ith one-shot models. SPECTRE outperforms state-of-the-art deep autoregressi
 ve generators in terms of modeling fidelity\, while also avoiding expensive
  sequential generation and dependence on node ordering. A case in point\, i
 n sizable synthetic and real-world graphs SPECTRE achieves a 4-to-170 fold 
 improvement over the best competitor that does not overfit and is 23-to-30 
 times faster than autoregressive generators.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Detai
 ls:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST 
 / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=Z
 zlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDN
 ThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and pa
 per voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt
 -u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/sha
 red_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>A
 ll information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b>
 <b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https
 ://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></h
 tml-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195616Z
