ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=he
 li.benhamu@weizmann.ac.il;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:heli.benhamu@weizmann.ac.il
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240506T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Heli Ben-Hamu who is a PhD student at
  Weizmann Institute in Israel working with Yaron Lipman.<br><br><b>Paper:</
 b><br><b>D-Flow: Differentiating through Flows for Controlled Generation </
 b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.14017"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.
 14017</u></a> (Heli Ben-Hamu\, Omri Puny\, Itai Gat\, Brian Karrer\, Uriel 
 Singer\, Yaron Lipman)<br>Taming the generation outcome of state of the art
  Diffusion and Flow-Matching (FM) models without having to re-train a task-
 specific model unlocks a powerful tool for solving inverse problems\, condi
 tional generation\, and controlled generation in general. In this work we i
 ntroduce D-Flow\, a simple framework for controlling the generation process
  by differentiating through the flow\, optimizing for the source (noise) po
 int. We motivate this framework by our key observation stating that for Dif
 fusion/FM models trained with Gaussian probability paths\, differentiating 
 through the generation process projects gradient on the data manifold\, imp
 licitly injecting the prior into the optimization process. We validate our 
 framework on linear and non-linear controlled generation problems including
 : image and audio inverse problems and conditional molecule generation reac
 hing state of the art performance across all.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Deta
 ils:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST /
  8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUD
 ZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2
 JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<b
 r></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FH
 wX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n
 3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upco
 ming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://
 hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-readin
 g-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
