DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220201T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220201T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20220118T160000@google.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/ycq-aozn-xwf
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220201T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speakers:<br></b>Not author of the 
 paper: Hannes Stärk. Hey\, that's me :D<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Roto-tra
 nslated Local Coordinate Frames For Interacting Dynamical Systems</b>&nbsp\
 ;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14961" class="paper-link" style="displ
 ay: inline-block\;"><div class="paper-link-emoji">📎https://arxiv.org/abs/2
 110.14961</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author
 &query=Kofinas%2C+M">Miltiadis Kofinas</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.o
 rg/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Nagaraja%2C+N+S">Naveen Shankar Nagara
 ja</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query
 =Gavves%2C+E">Efstratios Gavves</a>) 2021<br>Modelling interactions is crit
 ical in learning complex dynamical systems\, namely systems of interacting 
 objects with highly non-linear and time-dependent behaviour. A large class 
 of such systems can be formalized as&nbsp\;geometric graphs\,&nbsp\;i.e.\, 
 graphs with nodes positioned in the Euclidean space given an&nbsp\;arbitrar
 ily&nbsp\;chosen global coordinate system\, for instance vehicles in a traf
 fic scene. Notwithstanding the arbitrary global coordinate system\, the gov
 erning dynamics of the respective dynamical systems are invariant to rotati
 ons and translations\, also known as&nbsp\;Galilean invariance. As ignoring
  these invariances leads to worse generalization\, in this work we propose 
 local coordinate frames per node-object to induce roto-translation invarian
 ce to the geometric graph of the interacting dynamical system. Further\, th
 e local coordinate frames allow for a natural definition of anisotropic fil
 tering in graph neural networks. Experiments in traffic scenes\, 3D motion 
 capture\, and colliding particles demonstrate that the proposed approach co
 mfortably outperforms the recent state-of-the-art.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting
  Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PT<
 /i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm
 5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</
 a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a hre
 f="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXv
 xLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mb
 o1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule 
 of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="h
 ttps://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag
 -reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
 \nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/ycq-aozn-xwf\n\nLearn more
  about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease
  do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
