BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20260216T180000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20260216T190000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob_R20250630T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ja
 sonkyuyim@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:jasonkyuyim@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=michae
 lsalbergo@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:michaelsalbergo@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=pe
 ter.potaptchik@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:peter.potaptchik@gmail.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20260216T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Peter Pot
 aptchik who is a DPhil student in the Department of Statistics at the Unive
 rsity of Oxford\, advised by <a href="https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/~deligian/
 " target="_blank">George Deligiannidis</a>\, <a href="https://www.saifsyed.
 com/" target="_blank">Saifuddin Syed</a>\, and <a href="https://www.stats.o
 x.ac.uk/~teh/" target="_blank">Yee Whye Teh</a>. Currently he is visiting M
 ichael Albergo at Harvard University.<br><b><br></b><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b
 >Meta Flow Maps enable scalable reward alignment </b><a href="https://arxiv
 .org/abs/2601.14430">https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.14430</a> <b>(</b>Peter Pot
 aptchik\, Adhi Saravanan\, Abbas Mammadov\, Alvaro Prat\, Michael S. Alberg
 o\, Yee Whye Teh)<br>Controlling generative models is computationally expen
 sive. This is because optimal alignment with a reward function--whether via
  inference-time steering or fine-tuning--requires estimating the value func
 tion. This task demands access to the conditional posterior p1|t(x1|xt)\, t
 he distribution of clean data x1 consistent with an intermediate state xt\,
  a requirement that typically compels methods to resort to costly trajector
 y simulations. To address this bottleneck\, we introduce Meta Flow Maps (MF
 Ms)\, a framework extending consistency models and flow maps into the stoch
 astic regime. MFMs are trained to perform stochastic one-step posterior sam
 pling\, generating arbitrarily many i.i.d. draws of clean data x1 from any 
 intermediate state. Crucially\, these samples provide a differentiable repa
 rametrization that unlocks efficient value function estimation. We leverage
  this capability to solve bottlenecks in both paradigms: enabling inference
 -time steering without inner rollouts\, and facilitating unbiased\, off-pol
 icy fine-tuning to general rewards. Empirically\, our single-particle steer
 ed-MFM sampler outperforms a Best-of-1000 baseline on ImageNet across multi
 ple rewards at a fraction of the compute.<br><b><br></b><br><b><br></b><br>
 <b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  
 18:00 CE(S)T  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNTh
 hUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=Zzl
 GTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion 
 and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_inv
 ite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg" target="_blank"><u>https://join.sl
 ack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg</u></a><b
 r><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailin
 g list</b><b>:<br></b><a href="https://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaki
 ng" target="_blank">https://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking</a><b></
 b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
