DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20251027T180000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20251027T190000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob_R20250630T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ye
 hlin@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:yehlin@mit.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20251201T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Yehlin Ch
 o who is a PhD student at MIT working with Sergey Ovchinnikov.<br><br><b>Pa
 per:</b><br><b>Protein Hunter: exploiting structure hallucination within di
 ffusion for protein design </b><a href="https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.
 1101/2025.10.10.681530v2">https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.10.1
 0.681530v2</a> ( Yehlin Cho\, Griffin Rangel\,  Gaurav Bhardwaj\, Sergey Ov
 chinnikov)<br>Interactions between proteins and other biomolecules underlie
  nearly all biological processes\, yet designing such interactions de novo 
 remains challenging. Capturing their specific interactions and co-optimizin
 g sequence and structure are difficult and often require extensive computat
 ion. We present Protein Hunter\, a fast\, fine-tuning-free framework for de
  novo protein design. Starting from an all-X sequence\, we find diffusion-b
 ased structure prediction models hallucinate reasonable looking structures 
 that can be further improved through iterative sequence re-design and struc
 ture re-prediction. This lightweight strategy achieves high AlphaFold3 in s
 ilico success rates across both unconditional and conditional generation ta
 sks\, including binders to proteins\, cyclic peptides\, small molecules\, D
 NA\, and RNA. Protein Hunter also supports multi-motif scaffolding and part
 ial redesign\, providing a general and efficient platform for de novo prote
 in design across diverse molecular targets.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Detail
 s:<br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i
 ><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5p
 QT09" target="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4v
 N2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:
 <br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-
 rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg" target="_blank"><u>https://join.slack.com/t/logag/s
 hared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg</u></a><br><br><b>All info
 rmation: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br
 ></b><a href="https://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking" target="_blan
 k">https://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking</a><b></b><u></u><u></u><
 u></u><u></u><u></u>
