CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the paper <a href
 ="https://fedelopez77.github.io/" id="ow639" __is_owner="true">Federico Lóp
 ez</a> who is a Ph.D candidate in&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.h-its.org/">HI
 TS</a>&nbsp\;at Heidelberg University. Prior to this\, he studied Software 
 Engineering at&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.fi.uba.ar/">University of Buenos A
 ires</a>.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Symmetric Spaces for Graph Embeddings:
  A Finsler-Riemannian Approach</b>&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/210
 6.04941">https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.04941</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv
 .org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=L%C3%B3pez%2C+F">Federico López
 </a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;qu
 ery=Pozzetti%2C+B">Beatrice Pozzetti</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Trettel%2C+S">Steve Trettel</a>\,&n
 bsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Stru
 be%2C+M">Michael Strube</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?se
 archtype=author&amp\;query=Wienhard%2C+A">Anna Wienhard</a>) 2021<br>Learni
 ng faithful graph representations as sets of vertex embeddings has become a
  fundamental intermediary step in a wide range of machine learning applicat
 ions. We propose the systematic use of symmetric spaces in representation l
 earning\, a class encompassing many of the previously used embedding target
 s. This enables us to introduce a new method\, the use of Finsler metrics i
 ntegrated in a Riemannian optimization scheme\, that better adapts to dissi
 milar structures in the graph. We develop a tool to analyze the embeddings 
 and infer structural properties of the data sets. For implementation\, we c
 hoose Siegel spaces\, a versatile family of symmetric spaces. Our approach 
 outperforms competitive baselines for graph reconstruction tasks on various
  synthetic and real-world datasets. We further demonstrate its applicabilit
 y on two downstream tasks\, recommender systems and node classification.<br
 ><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET / 4pm UT
 C / 11am EDT / 8am PT</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlG
 TXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThh
 UDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper
  voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0
 mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared
 _invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All 
 information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>
 :<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://
 hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b></html-blob>
