BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221121T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221121T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20221107T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=zh
 angjiy20@mails.tsinghua.edu.cn;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:zhangjiy20@mails.tsing
 hua.edu.cn
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221121T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></
 b>The first author of the paper&nbsp\;<a href="https://youjibiying.github.i
 o/">Jiying Zhang</a> who is an MS student at Tsinghua University&nbsp\;<u><
 /u><span>co-advised by Xi Xiao and Shu-Tao Xia.&nbsp\;</span><span>He previ
 ously did an internship at Tencent AI Lab.</span><br><u></u><br><b>Paper:</
 b><br>Fine-Tuning Graph Neural Networks via Graph Topology induced Optimal 
 Transport&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.10453" class="paper-lin
 k" style="display: inline-block\;">https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.10453</a>&nbs
 p\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Zhang%2C+J
 ">Jiying Zhang</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=
 author&query=Xiao%2C+X">Xi Xiao</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/sear
 ch/cs?searchtype=author&query=Huang%2C+L">Long-Kai Huang</a>\,&nbsp\;<a hre
 f="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Rong%2C+Y">Yu Rong</
 a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Bia
 n%2C+Y">Yatao Bian</a>)<br>Recently\, the pretrain-finetuning paradigm has 
 attracted tons of attention in graph learning community due to its power of
  alleviating the lack of labels problem in many real-world applications. Cu
 rrent studies use existing techniques\, such as weight constraint\, represe
 ntation constraint\, which are derived from images or text data\, to transf
 er the invariant knowledge from the pre-train stage to fine-tuning stage. H
 owever\, these methods failed to preserve invariances from graph structure 
 and Graph Neural Network (GNN) style models. In this paper\, we present a n
 ovel optimal transport-based fine-tuning framework called GTOT-Tuning\, nam
 ely\, Graph Topology induced Optimal Transport fine-Tuning\, for GNN style 
 backbones. GTOT-Tuning is required to utilize the property of graph data to
  enhance the preservation of representation produced by fine-tuned networks
 . Toward this goal\, we formulate graph local knowledge transfer as an Opti
 mal Transport (OT) problem with a structural prior and construct the GTOT r
 egularizer to constrain the fine-tuned model behaviors. By using the adjace
 ncy relationship amongst nodes\, the GTOT regularizer achieves node-level o
 ptimal transport procedures and reduces redundant transport procedures\, re
 sulting in efficient knowledge transfer from the pre-trained models. We eva
 luate GTOT-Tuning on eight downstream tasks with various GNN backbones and 
 demonstrate that it achieves state-of-the-art fine-tuning performance for G
 NNs.<b><br><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i
 ><i>5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="h
 ttps://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://z
 oom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slac
 k Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.s
 lack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https:/
 /join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</
 a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, ma
 iling list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-readin
 g-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u>
 </u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
