BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20230306T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20230306T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20230102T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ju
 lius.berner@univie.ac.at;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:julius.berner@univie.ac.at
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20230306T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="
 https://jberner.info/">Julius Berner</a> who is a PhD student at the Univer
 sity of Vienna.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>An optimal control perspective o
 n diffusion-based generative modeling</b><br> <a href="https://arxiv.org/ab
 s/2211.01364">https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.01364</a> (Julius Berner\, Lorenz 
 Richter\, Karen Ullrich)<br>We establish a connection between stochastic op
 timal control and generative models based on stochastic differential equati
 ons (SDEs) such as recently developed diffusion probabilistic models. In pa
 rticular\, we derive a Hamilton-Jacobi-Bellman equation that governs the ev
 olution of the log-densities of the underlying SDE marginals. This perspect
 ive allows to transfer methods from optimal control theory to generative mo
 deling. First\, we show that the evidence lower bound is a direct consequen
 ce of the well-known verification theorem from control theory. Further\, we
  develop a novel diffusion-based method for sampling from unnormalized dens
 ities -- a problem frequently occurring in statistics and computational sci
 ences.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> <
 /i><i>5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoo
 m.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5
 775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspac
 e for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t
 /logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slac
 k.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br>
 <b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list
 </b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">h
 ttps://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u
 ><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250330T035026Z
