ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ak
 hilprem@uchicago.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:akhilprem@uchicago.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20241125T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Akhil Pre
 mkumar who works on theoretic aspects of de Sitter (dS) space\, and its rel
 ation to the physics of inflation. <br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Neural Entro
 py </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.03817">https://arxiv.org/abs/240
 9.03817</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;qu
 ery=Premkumar\,+A">Akhil Premkumar</a>)<br>We examine the connection betwee
 n deep learning and information theory through the paradigm of diffusion mo
 dels. Using well-established principles from non-equilibrium thermodynamics
  we can characterize the amount of information required to reverse a diffus
 ive process. Neural networks store this information and operate in a manner
  reminiscent of Maxwell's demon during the generative stage. We illustrate 
 this cycle using a novel diffusion scheme we call the entropy matching mode
 l\, wherein the information conveyed to the network during training exactly
  corresponds to the entropy that must be negated during reversal. We demons
 trate that this entropy can be used to analyze the encoding efficiency and 
 storage capacity of the network. This conceptual picture blends elements of
  stochastic optimal control\, thermodynamics\, information theory\, and opt
 imal transport\, and raises the prospect of applying diffusion models as a 
 test bench to understand neural networks.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:
 <br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i><
 br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT
 09" target="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2
 JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<b
 r></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2nmy5vsj7-8K
 EDXe~mU~p5fCxwupSv5w" target="_blank">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared
 _invite/zt-2nmy5vsj7-8KEDXe~mU~p5fCxwupSv5w</a><br><br><b>All information: 
 Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><a h
 ref="https://portal.valencelabs.com/logg" target="_blank">https://portal.va
 lencelabs.com/logg</a><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
