DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220906T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220906T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ji
 .hou@tum.de;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:ji.hou@tum.de
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=xi
 esaining@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:xiesaining@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=be
 njamingraham@fb.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:benjamingraham@fb.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220906T170000
CREATED:20220820T195614Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Dr <a href="https:/
 /sekunde.github.io/" id="ow491" __is_owner="true">Ji Hou</a>&nbsp\;who is a
  Research Scientist at Meta Reality Labs. Previously\, he did his Ph.D. at 
 the TUM Visual Computing Group headed by&nbsp\;<a href="https://niessnerlab
 .org/members/matthias_niessner/profile.html">Prof. Matthias Niessner</a>\, 
 where he worked on Computer Vision and 3D Scene Understanding.<br><br><b>Pa
 per:</b><br><b>Pri3D: Can 3D Priors Help 2D Representation Learning?</b>&nb
 sp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.11225" class="paper-link" style="di
 splay: inline-block\;">https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.11225</a>&nbsp\;(<a href=
 "https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Hou%2C+J" class="
 paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Ji Hou</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Xie%2C+S" class="pape
 r-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Saining Xie</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="ht
 tps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Graham%2C+B" class="
 paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Benjamin Graham</a>\,&nbsp\;<a 
 href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Dai%2C+A" cl
 ass="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Angela Dai</a>\,&nbsp\;<a 
 href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Nie%C3%9Fner
 %2C+M" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Matthias Nießner<
 /a>)<br>Recent advances in 3D perception have shown impressive progress in 
 understanding geometric structures of 3Dshapes and even scenes. Inspired by
  these advances in geometric understanding\, we aim to imbue image-based pe
 rception with representations learned under geometric constraints. We intro
 duce an approach to learn view-invariant\,geometry-aware representations fo
 r network pre-training\, based on multi-view RGB-D data\, that can then be 
 effectively transferred to downstream 2D tasks. We propose to employ contra
 stive learning under both multi-view im-age constraints and image-geometry 
 constraints to encode3D priors into learned 2D representations. This result
 s not only in improvement over 2D-only representation learning on the image
 -based tasks of semantic segmentation\, instance segmentation\, and object 
 detection on real-world in-door datasets\, but moreover\, provides signific
 ant improvement in the low data regime. We show a significant improvement o
 f 6.0% on semantic segmentation on full data as well as 11.9% on 20% data a
 gainst baselines on ScanNet.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Ev
 ery Tuesday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\
 ;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOd
 U4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRM
 m5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br><
 /b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd
 1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u
 ></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: 
 Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><
 a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.
 com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220906T154938Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
