 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20210824T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=email@
 matej-z.de;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:email@matej-z.de
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=pe
 tarv@google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:petarv@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20211109T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:<br></b>First author&nbsp\;<a href="https://matej-ze
 cevic.de/">Matej Zečević</a>&nbsp\;who is a PhD candidate at TU Darmstadt w
 orking with&nbsp\;<a href="https://ml-research.github.io/people/kkersting/i
 ndex.html">Kristian Kersting</a>&nbsp\;on Causality for ML.&nbsp\;Before th
 at\, he completed his M.Sc. in Computer Science under&nbsp\;<a href="https:
 //www.ias.informatik.tu-darmstadt.de/Member/JanPeters">Jan Peters</a>\,&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://cifar.ca/bios/stefan-bauer/">Stefan Bauer</a>\, and&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://www.is.mpg.de/~bs">Bernhard Schölkopf&nbsp\;</a>at MPI 
 for Intelligent Systems (Tübingen).<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Relating Gra
 ph Neural Networks to Structural Causal Models&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://a
 rxiv.org/abs/2109.04173">https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.04173</a>&nbsp\;(<a hre
 f="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Ze%C4%8Devi%C4%87%2C
 +M">Matej Zečević</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchty
 pe=author&query=Dhami%2C+D+S">Devendra Singh Dhami</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Veli%C4%8Dkovi%C4%87%2C+P"
 >Petar Veličković</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchty
 pe=author&query=Kersting%2C+K">Kristian Kersting</a>)<br>Causality can be d
 escribed in terms of a structural causal model (SCM) that carries informati
 on on the variables of interest and their mechanistic relations. For most p
 rocesses of interest the underlying SCM will only be partially observable\,
  thus causal inference tries to leverage any exposed information. Graph neu
 ral networks (GNN) as universal approximators on structured input pose a vi
 able candidate for causal learning\, suggesting a tighter integration with 
 SCM. To this effect we present a theoretical analysis from first principles
  that establishes a novel connection between GNN and SCM while providing an
  extended view on general neural-causal models. We then establish a new mod
 el class for GNN-based causal inference that is necessary and sufficient fo
 r causal effect identification. Our empirical illustration on simulations a
 nd standard benchmarks validate our theoretical proofs.<br><b><br></b><b>Me
 eting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8a
 m PT</i><br><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/4556095405?pwd=UmZRbC95d050T
 kRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09" id="ow1273" __is_owner="true">https://us02web.zoom.us/
 j/4556095405?pwd=UmZRbC95d050TkRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09</a><br><br><b>Join Slack 
 Workspace for discussions beyond the meetings and paper voting:<br></b><a h
 ref="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGj
 XvxLSokvg" id="ow1277" __is_owner="true">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>lo
 gag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><
 br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming talks\, slides + notes of previ
 ously covered papers</b><b>:<br></b><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag
 -reading-group" id="ow1287" __is_owner="true">https://hannes-stark.com/loga
 g-reading-group</a><b><br></b>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195612Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learning on Graphs and Geometry Reading Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
