DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240304T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=aelhag
 @aimsammi.org;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:aelhag@aimsammi.org
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240304T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Ahmed Elh
 ag wo is currently a PhD student in Computer Science at University of Oxfor
 d. His research areas include graph ML and geometric deep learning\, with v
 arious applications in computational chemistry\, drug discovery and design.
 <br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Manifold Diffusion Fields </b><a href="https://
 arxiv.org/abs/2305.15586">https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15586</a> (<a href="ht
 tps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Elhag\,+A+A">Ahmed A
 . Elhag</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;q
 uery=Susskind\,+J+M">Joshua M. Susskind</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/se
 arch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bautista\,+M+A">Miguel Angel Bautista<
 /a>)<br>We present Manifold Diffusion Fields (MDF)\, an approach to learn g
 enerative models of continuous functions defined over Riemannian manifolds.
  Leveraging insights from spectral geometry analysis\, we define an intrins
 ic coordinate system on the manifold via the eigen-functions of the Laplace
 -Beltrami Operator. MDF represents functions using an explicit parametrizat
 ion formed by a set of multiple input-output pairs. Our approach allows to 
 sample continuous functions on manifolds and is invariant with respect to r
 igid and isometric transformations of the manifold. Empirical results on se
 veral datasets and manifolds show that MDF can capture distributions of suc
 h functions with better diversity and fidelity than previous approaches.<br
 ><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm
  CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/57
 75722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530
 ?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for dis
 cussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/sh
 ared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/l
 ogag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All in
 formation: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<
 br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://ha
 nnes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><
 u></u><u></u>
