ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20221003T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=larsho
 ldijk@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:larsholdijk@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=pj
 aini@google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:pjaini@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221010T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Authors&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://www.larsholdijk.com/"><u>Lars Holdijk</u></a>&nbsp\;and Dr.&nbsp\;<a h
 ref="https://priyankjaini.github.io/"><u>Priyank Jaini</u></a>. Lars is an 
 ELLIS Program MSc student of Prof. Max Welling at University of Amsterdam a
 nd Prof. Yarin Gal at University of Oxford. Dr Jaini is a Research Scientis
 t in the Brain team at&nbsp\;<a href="https://ai.google/research"><u>Google
  Research</u></a>&nbsp\;in Toronto and before that he was a PostDoc of Prof
 . Welling.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Learning Equivariant Energy Based Mod
 els with Equivariant Stein Variational Gradient Descent&nbsp\;</b><a href="
 https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.07832" class="paper-link" style="display: inline
 -block\;"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.07832</u></a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https
 ://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Jaini%2C+P"><u>Priyank Jaini
 </u></a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&que
 ry=Holdijk%2C+L"><u>Lars Holdijk</u></a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Welling%2C+M"><u>Max Welling</u></a>)<br
 >We focus on the problem of efficient sampling and learning of probability 
 densities by incorporating symmetries in probabilistic models. We first int
 roduce Equivariant Stein Variational Gradient Descent algorithm -- an equiv
 ariant sampling method based on Stein's identity for sampling from densitie
 s with symmetries. Equivariant SVGD explicitly incorporates symmetry inform
 ation in a density through equivariant kernels which makes the resultant sa
 mpler efficient both in terms of sample complexity and the quality of gener
 ated samples. Subsequently\, we define equivariant energy based models to m
 odel invariant densities that are learned using contrastive divergence. By 
 utilizing our equivariant SVGD for training equivariant EBMs\, we propose n
 ew ways of improving and scaling up training of energy based models. We app
 ly these equivariant energy models for modelling joint densities in regress
 ion and classification tasks for image datasets\, many-body particle system
 s and molecular structure generation.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br>
 </b><i>Every Monday at</i><i>&nbsp\;</i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 
 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=Zzl
 GTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09"><u>https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlD
 NThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</u></a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion a
 nd paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invi
 te/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shar
 ed_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All information
 : Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u
 ><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group"><u>https://hannes-s
 tark.com/logag-reading-group</u></a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learning on Graphs and Geometry Reading Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
