BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240408T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240408T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=sanjee
 vr@berkeley.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:sanjeevr@berkeley.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240408T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Sanjeev w
 ho is a CS PhD student at UC Berkeley advised by Aditi Krishnapriyan.<br><b
 r><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Stability-Aware Training of Neural Network Interatomi
 c Potentials with Differentiable Boltzmann Estimators </b><a href="https://
 arxiv.org/abs/2402.13984">https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.13984</a> (<a href="ht
 tps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Raja\,+S"><u>Sanjeev
  Raja</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\
 ;query=Amin\,+I">Ishan Amin</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?sear
 chtype=author&amp\;query=Pedregosa\,+F">Fabian Pedregosa</a>\, <a href="htt
 ps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Krishnapriyan\,+A+S">
 Aditi S. Krishnapriyan</a>)<br>Neural network interatomic potentials (NNIPs
 ) are an attractive alternative to ab-initio methods for molecular dynamics
  (MD) simulations. However\, they can produce unstable simulations which sa
 mple unphysical states\, limiting their usefulness for modeling phenomena o
 ccurring over longer timescales. To address these challenges\, we present S
 tability-Aware Boltzmann Estimator (StABlE) Training\, a multi-modal traini
 ng procedure which combines conventional supervised training from quantum-m
 echanical energies and forces with reference system observables\, to produc
 e stable and accurate NNIPs. StABlE Training iteratively runs MD simulation
 s to seek out unstable regions\, and corrects the instabilities via supervi
 sion with a reference observable. The training procedure is enabled by the 
 Boltzmann Estimator\, which allows efficient computation of gradients requi
 red to train neural networks to system observables\, and can detect both gl
 obal and local instabilities. We demonstrate our methodology across organic
  molecules\, tetrapeptides\, and condensed phase systems\, along with using
  three modern NNIP architectures. In all three cases\, StABlE-trained model
 s achieve significant improvements in simulation stability and recovery of 
 structural and dynamic observables. In some cases\, StABlE-trained models o
 utperform conventional models trained on datasets 50 times larger. As a gen
 eral framework applicable across NNIP architectures and systems\, StABlE Tr
 aining is a powerful tool for training stable and accurate NNIPs\, particul
 arly in the absence of large reference datasets.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting D
 etails:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am ES
 T / 8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNTh
 hUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4
 vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting
 :<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a
 -FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22
 y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of u
 pcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https
 ://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-rea
 ding-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
