BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20211019T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20211019T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20210824T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ua
 lon@cs.cmu.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:ualon@cs.cmu.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=urialo
 n1@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:urialon1@gmail.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/qzb-teus-afh
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20211019T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the paper Dr.&nbsp\;<a href=
 "https://urialon.ml/">Uri Alon</a>&nbsp\;who&nbsp\;obtained my PhD at Techn
 ion (Israel)\, advised by&nbsp\;Prof.&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.cs.technio
 n.ac.il/~yahave/">Eran Yahav</a>. He is now a Postdoctoral Researcher at th
 e Language Technologies Institute of Carnegie Mellon University\, working w
 ith Prof.&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.phontron.com/">Graham Neubig</a>&nbsp\;
 on NLP and learning from source code\, where GNNs find many applications. M
 y most recent GNN work includes "<a href="https://openreview.net/pdf?id=i80
 OPhOCVH2">On the Bottleneck of Graph Neural Networks and its Practical Impl
 ications</a>" and "<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2105.14491.pdf">How Atten
 tive are Graph Attention Networks?</a>". His personal website is at&nbsp\;<
 a href="http://urialon.ml/" id="ow464" __is_owner="true">urialon.ml</a><br>
 <br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>On the Bottleneck of Graph Neural Networks and its 
 Practical Implications&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.05205"
 >https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.05205</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/sea
 rch/cs?searchtype=author&query=Alon%2C+U">Uri Alon</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Yahav%2C+E">Eran Yahav</a>
 )<br>Since the proposal of the graph neural network (GNN) by Gori et al. (2
 005) and Scarselli et al. (2008)\, one of the major problems in training GN
 Ns was their struggle to propagate information between distant nodes in the
  graph. We propose a new explanation for this problem: GNNs are susceptible
  to a bottleneck when aggregating messages across a long path. This bottlen
 eck causes the over-squashing of exponentially growing information into fix
 ed-size vectors. As a result\, GNNs fail to propagate messages originating 
 from distant nodes and perform poorly when the prediction task depends on l
 ong-range interaction. In this paper\, we highlight the inherent problem of
  over-squashing in GNNs: we demonstrate that the bottleneck hinders popular
  GNNs from fitting long-range signals in the training data\; we further sho
 w that GNNs that absorb incoming edges equally\, such as GCN and GIN\, are 
 more susceptible to over-squashing than GAT and GGNN\; finally\, we show th
 at prior work\, which extensively tuned GNN models of long-range problems\,
  suffers from over-squashing\, and that breaking the bottleneck improves th
 eir state-of-the-art results without any tuning or additional weights. Our 
 code is available at&nbsp\;<a href="https://github.com/tech-srl/bottleneck/
 ">this https URL</a>&nbsp\;.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Ev
 ery Tuesday at 5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST</i><br><a href="http
 s://us02web.zoom.us/j/4556095405?pwd=UmZRbC95d050TkRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09" id="
 ow482" __is_owner="true">https://us02web.zoom.us/j/4556095405?pwd=UmZRbC95d
 050TkRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09</a><br><br><b>Join Slack Workspace for discussions 
 beyond the meetings and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.co
 m/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.sl
 ack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXG
 jXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming talks\, slid
 es + notes of previously covered papers</b><b>:<br></b><a href="http:///">h
 ttps://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a><b><br></b>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\
 nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/qzb-teus-afh\n\nLearn more 
 about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease 
 do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
