UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=frey.n
 athan.nf1@gene.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:frey.nathan.nf1@gene.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240212T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Nathan C.
  Frey. His bio: <span>I am a Machine Learning Scientist and Group Leader at
  </span><a href="https://www.gene.com/scientists/our-scientists/prescient-d
 esign"><u>Prescient Design</u></a><span> </span><span>•</span><span> </span
 ><a href="https://www.gene.com/scientists/our-scientists/nathan-frey"><u>Ge
 nentech</u></a><span>. At Prescient\, my focus is on developing and applyin
 g machine learning methods to protein design. I have a PhD in Materials Sci
 ence &amp\; Engineering from the</span><span> </span><a href="https://www.u
 penn.edu/"><u>University of Pennsylvania</u></a><span>. I use multiscale mo
 deling and machine learning to design materials and molecules. My research 
 spans condensed matter physics\, chemistry\, biology\, computation\, and au
 tomation. I have published more than 20 scientific papers in journals such 
 as</span><span> </span><em>Science Advances</em><span>\,</span><span> </spa
 n><em>ACS Nano</em><span>\,</span><span> </span><em>JACS</em><span>\, and</
 span><span> </span><em>Chemistry of Materials</em><span>. </span><span>I co
 -founded</span><span> </span><a href="https://www.atomicdatasciences.com/">
 <u>Atomic Data Sciences</u></a><span> </span><span>to provide data manageme
 nt and analysis software for nanotech companies. </span><span>Previously\, 
 I was a Postdoctoral Associate at</span><span> </span><a href="https://web.
 mit.edu/"><u>MIT</u></a><span> </span><span>working with the</span><span> <
 /span><a href="https://www.ll.mit.edu/r-d/cyber-security-and-information-sc
 iences/lincoln-laboratory-supercomputing-center"><u>Lincoln Lab Supercomput
 ing</u></a><span> </span><span>and</span><span> </span><a href="https://www
 .ll.mit.edu/r-d/cyber-security-and-information-sciences/artificial-intellig
 ence-technology-and-systems"><u>AI</u></a><span> </span><span>groups. I was
  a</span><span> </span><a href="https://ndseg.sysplus.com/NDSEG/About/"><u>
 National Defense Science &amp\; Engineering Graduate Fellow</u></a><span> <
 /span><span>in the</span><span> </span><a href="http://shenoy.seas.upenn.ed
 u/"><u>Shenoy group</u></a><span> </span><span>at UPenn and an affiliate sc
 ientist with Kristin Persson’s</span><span> </span><a href="https://materia
 lsproject.org/about"><u>Materials Project</u></a><span> </span><span>group 
 at</span><span> </span><a href="https://www.lbl.gov/"><u>Berkeley Lab</u></
 a><span>.</span><span><br></span><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Protein Discovery 
 with Discrete Walk-Jump Sampling </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12
 360">https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.12360</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/searc
 h/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Frey\,+N+C">Nathan C. Frey</a>\, <a hr
 ef="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Berenberg\,
 +D">Daniel Berenberg</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchty
 pe=author&amp\;query=Zadorozhny\,+K">Karina Zadorozhny</a>\, <a href="https
 ://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Kleinhenz\,+J">Josep
 h Kleinhenz</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author
 &amp\;query=Lafrance-Vanasse\,+J">Julien Lafrance-Vanasse</a>\, <a href="ht
 tps://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Hotzel\,+I">Isidr
 o Hotzel</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&am
 p\;query=Wu\,+Y">Yan Wu</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searc
 htype=author&amp\;query=Ra\,+S">Stephen Ra</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bonneau\,+R">Richard Bonneau</a>
 \, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Cho
 \,+K">Kyunghyun Cho</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtyp
 e=author&amp\;query=Loukas\,+A">Andreas Loukas</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv
 .org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Gligorijevic\,+V">Vladimir G
 ligorijevic</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author
 &amp\;query=Saremi\,+S">Saeed Saremi</a>)<br>We resolve difficulties in tra
 ining and sampling from a discrete generative model by learning a smoothed 
 energy function\, sampling from the smoothed data manifold with Langevin Ma
 rkov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC)\, and projecting back to the true data manifo
 ld with one-step denoising. Our Discrete Walk-Jump Sampling formalism combi
 nes the maximum likelihood training of an energy-based model and improved s
 ample quality of a score-based model\, while simplifying training and sampl
 ing by requiring only a single noise level. We evaluate the robustness of o
 ur approach on generative modeling of antibody proteins and introduce the d
 istributional conformity score to benchmark protein generative models. By o
 ptimizing and sampling from our models for the proposed distributional conf
 ormity score\, 97-100% of generated samples are successfully expressed and 
 purified and 35% of functional designs show equal or improved binding affin
 ity compared to known functional antibodies on the first attempt in a singl
 e round of laboratory experiments. We also report the first demonstration o
 f long-run fast-mixing MCMC chains where diverse antibody protein classes a
 re visited in a single MCMC chain.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b
 ><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  
 </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRM
 m5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09<
 /a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a hr
 ef="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZC
 a0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31
 gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers
 \, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-star
 k.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group<br>
 </a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
