DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240311T160000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240311T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=Zahra 
 Kadkhodaie;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:zk388@nyu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240311T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Zahra Kad
 khodaie is a PhD student of Data Science at NYU (advised by Prof. Eero Simo
 ncelli) and a guest researcher in the Center for Computational Neuroscience
 . Her research focuses on understanding and improving deep neural networks 
 by analyzing and imposing mathematical symmetries on the architecture. More
  recently\, she has worked on extracting and utilizing the prior embedded i
 n a trained deep neural network denoiser for solving other computer vision 
 problems without further training. Zahra completed her B.Sc. in Solid State
  Physics at K.N. Toosi University in Tehran\, Iran and her M.Sc in Data Sci
 ence and Psychology at NYU.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Generalization in di
 ffusion models arises from geometry-adaptive harmonic representation </b><a
  href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.02557#:~:text=Generalization%20in%20diffu
 sion%20models%20arises%20from%20geometry%2Dadaptive%20harmonic%20representa
 tion\,-Zahra%20Kadkhodaie%2C%20Florentin&amp\;text=High%2Dquality%20samples
 %20generated%20with\,despite%20the%20curse%20of%20dimensionality.">https://
 arxiv.org/abs/2310.02557</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchty
 pe=author&amp\;query=Kadkhodaie\,+Z">Zahra Kadkhodaie</a><span>\,</span><sp
 an> </span><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;quer
 y=Guth\,+F">Florentin Guth</a><span>\,</span><span> </span><a href="https:/
 /arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Simoncelli\,+E+P">Eero P.
  Simoncelli</a><span>\,</span><span> </span><a href="https://arxiv.org/sear
 ch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Mallat\,+S">Stéphane Mallat</a>)<br>High
 -quality samples generated with score-based reverse diffusion algorithms pr
 ovide evidence that deep neural networks (DNN) trained for denoising can le
 arn high-dimensional densities\, despite the curse of dimensionality. Howev
 er\, recent reports of memorization of the training set raise the question 
 of whether these networks are learning the "true" continuous density of the
  data. Here\, we show that two denoising DNNs trained on non-overlapping su
 bsets of a dataset learn nearly the same score function\, and thus the same
  density\, with a surprisingly small number of training images. This strong
  generalization demonstrates an alignment of powerful inductive biases in t
 he DNN architecture and/or training algorithm with properties of the data d
 istribution. We analyze these\, demonstrating that the denoiser performs a 
 shrinkage operation in a basis adapted to the underlying image. Examination
  of these bases reveals oscillating harmonic structures along contours and 
 in homogeneous image regions. We show that trained denoisers are inductivel
 y biased towards these geometry-adaptive harmonic representations by demons
 trating that they arise even when the network is trained on image classes s
 uch as low-dimensional manifolds\, for which the harmonic basis is suboptim
 al. Additionally\, we show that the denoising performance of the networks i
 s near-optimal when trained on regular image classes for which the optimal 
 basis is known to be geometry-adaptive and harmonic.<br><br><b>Meeting Deta
 ils:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST /
  8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUD
 ZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2
 JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<b
 r></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FH
 wX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n
 3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upco
 ming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://
 hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-readin
 g-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
