DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220215T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220215T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20220118T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ma
 xistadler@gmx.net;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:maxistadler@gmx.net
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=charpe
 nt@in.tum.de;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:charpent@in.tum.de
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/rva-wxea-hys
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220215T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:<br></b>First authors <a href="https://maximilian-st
 adler.de/" id="ow1473" __is_owner="true">Maximilian Stadler</a> and <a href
 ="https://www.in.tum.de/en/daml/team/bertrand-charpentier/" id="ow1488" __i
 s_owner="true">Bertrand Charpentier</a>. Maximilian received his M.Sc. with
  high distinction from the Technical University of Munich. He wrote his the
 sis in the group of Prof. Günnemann. In this group\, Bertrand is a PhD cand
 idate working on uncertainty estimation and ML for graphs.<br><br><b>Paper:
 </b><br><b>Graph Posterior Network: Bayesian Predictive Uncertainty for Nod
 e Classification</b>&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14012">https
 ://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14012</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/st
 at?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Stadler%2C+M">Maximilian Stadler</a>\,&nbsp
 \;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Charp
 entier%2C+B">Bertrand Charpentier</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/se
 arch/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Geisler%2C+S">Simon Geisler</a>\,&nb
 sp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Z%C
 3%BCgner%2C+D">Daniel Zügner</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/
 stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=G%C3%BCnnemann%2C+S">Stephan Günnemann</a
 >)<br>The interdependence between nodes in graphs is key to improve class p
 redictions on nodes and utilized in approaches like Label Propagation (LP) 
 or in Graph Neural Networks (GNN). Nonetheless\, uncertainty estimation for
  non-independent node-level predictions is under-explored. In this work\, w
 e explore uncertainty quantification for node classification in three ways:
  (1) We derive three axioms explicitly characterizing the expected predicti
 ve uncertainty behavior in homophilic attributed graphs. (2) We propose a n
 ew model Graph Posterior Network (GPN) which explicitly performs Bayesian p
 osterior updates for predictions on interdependent nodes. GPN provably obey
 s the proposed axioms. (3) We extensively evaluate GPN and a strong set of 
 baselines on semi-supervised node classification including detection of ano
 malous features\, and detection of left-out classes. GPN outperforms existi
 ng approaches for uncertainty estimation in the experiments.<br><b><br></b>
 <b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET / 4pm UTC / 11am EDT
  / 8am PT</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZO
 dU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JR
 Mm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br>
 </b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmv
 d1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<
 u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information:
  Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u>
 <a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark
 .com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Goog
 le Meet: https://meet.google.com/rva-wxea-hys\n\nLearn more about Meet at: 
 https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease do not edit thi
 s section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
