UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=derekl
 im@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:dereklim@mit.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220517T170000
CREATED:20220820T195616Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="https://cp
 tq.github.io/" id="ow465" __is_owner="true"><u>Derek Lim</u></a>&nbsp\;who 
 is a PhD student in the group of Prof. Stefanie Jegelka at MIT. Derek previ
 ously presented <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.02910"><u>ESAN</u></a>&
 nbsp\;and Sign/Basis Nets in the reading group!<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br>The
 ory of Graph Neural Networks: Representation and Learning&nbsp\;<a href="ht
 tps://arxiv.org/abs/2204.07697" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-b
 lock\;">https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.07697</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.
 org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Jegelka%2C+S" class="paper-link"
  style="display: inline-block\;">Stefanie Jegelka</a>) 2022<br>Graph Neural
  Networks (GNNs)\, neural network architectures targeted to learning repres
 entations of graphs\, have become a popular learning model for prediction t
 asks on nodes\, graphs and configurations of points\, with wide success in 
 practice. This article summarizes a selection of the emerging theoretical r
 esults on approximation and learning properties of widely used message pass
 ing GNNs and higher-order GNNs\, focusing on representation\, generalizatio
 n and extrapolation. Along the way\, it summarizes mathematical connections
 .<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at</i><i> </i><
 i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="ht
 tps://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zo
 om.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack
  Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.sl
 ack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://j
 oin.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd
 1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers
 \, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-star
 k.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a>
 </u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
