DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20210824T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=lf
 aber@ethz.ch;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:lfaber@ethz.ch
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20210824T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the paper&nbsp\;<a href="htt
 ps://disco.ethz.ch/members/lfaber">Lukas Faber</a>&nbsp\;who is a PhD stude
 nt in the Distributed Computing Group at ETH Zürich supervised by Prof. Rog
 er Wattenhofer. He is also working at Google Zürich.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><b
 r><b>Should Graph Neural Networks Use Features\, Edges\, Or Both? </b><a hr
 ef="/" id="ow1677" __is_owner="true">https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.06857</a>&n
 bsp\;(Lukas Faber\, Yifan Lu\, Roger Wattenhofer)<br>Graph Neural Networks 
 (GNNs) are the first choice for learning algorithms on graph data. GNNs pro
 mise to integrate (i) node features as well as (ii) edge information in an 
 end-to-end learning algorithm. How does this promise work out practically? 
 In this paper\, we study to what extend GNNs are necessary to solve promine
 nt graph classification problems. We find that for graph classification\, a
  GNN is not more than the sum of its parts. We also find that\, unlike feat
 ures\, predictions with an edge-only model do not always transfer to GNNs.<
 br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CEST / 3pm
  UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST</i><br><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/4556095
 405?pwd=UmZRbC95d050TkRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09">https://us02web.zoom.us/j/4556095
 405?pwd=UmZRbC95d050TkRsZ2QvWER3SDdqUT09</a><br>Meeting ID: 455 609 5405<br
 >Passcode: logag<br><br><b>Join Slack Workspace for discussions beyond the 
 meetings and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/s
 hared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<
 u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg<
 /a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming talks\, slides + notes 
 of previously covered papers</b><b>:<br></b><a href="http:///">https://hann
 es-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a><b><br></b>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195612Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learning on Graphs and Geometry Reading Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
