CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Nicholas 
 Boffi who is an assistant professor at CMU.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>One-
 step Language Modeling via Continuous Denoising </b><a href="https://arxiv.
 org/abs/2602.16813">https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16813</a> (<a href="https://
 arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Lee\,+C">Chanhyuk Lee</a>\
 , <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Yoo\,+J
 ">Jaehoon Yoo</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&
 amp\;query=Agarwal\,+M">Manan Agarwal</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/sear
 ch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Shah\,+S">Sheel Shah</a>\, <a href="http
 s://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Huang\,+J">Jerry Huang
 </a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Ra
 ghunathan\,+A">Aditi Raghunathan</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs
 ?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Hong\,+S">Seunghoon Hong</a>\, <a href="https
 ://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Boffi\,+N+M">Nicholas M
 . Boffi</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;q
 uery=Kim\,+J">Jinwoo Kim</a>)<br>Language models based on discrete diffusio
 n have attracted widespread interest for their potential to provide faster 
 generation than autoregressive models. In practice\, however\, they exhibit
  a sharp degradation of sample quality in the few-step regime\, failing to 
 realize this promise. Here we show that language models leveraging flow-bas
 ed continuous denoising can outperform discrete diffusion in both quality a
 nd speed. By revisiting the fundamentals of flows over discrete modalities\
 , we build a flow-based language model (FLM) that performs Euclidean denois
 ing over one-hot token encodings. We show that the model can be trained by 
 predicting the clean data via a cross entropy objective\, where we introduc
 e a simple time reparameterization that greatly improves training stability
  and generation quality. By distilling FLM into its associated flow map\, w
 e obtain a distilled flow map language model (FMLM) capable of few-step gen
 eration. On the LM1B and OWT language datasets\, FLM attains generation qua
 lity matching state-of-the-art discrete diffusion models. With FMLM\, our a
 pproach outperforms recent few-step language models across the board\, with
  one-step generation exceeding their 8-step quality. Our work calls into qu
 estion the widely held hypothesis that discrete diffusion processes are nec
 essary for generative modeling over discrete modalities\, and paves the way
  toward accelerated flow-based language modeling at scale. Code is availabl
 e at this https URL.<br><br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every 
 Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i><br><a href="https
 ://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target="_blan
 k">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br
 ><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="ht
 tps://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsy
 Elg" target="_blank"><u>https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zu
 xi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg</u></a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule o
 f upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><a href="https
 ://portal.valencelabs.com/starklyspeaking" target="_blank">https://portal.v
 alencelabs.com/starklyspeaking</a><b></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u
 >
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T170220Z
