DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20221003T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=seul.l
 ee@kaist.ac.kr;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:seul.lee@kaist.ac.kr
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ha
 rryjo97@kaist.ac.kr;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:harryjo97@kaist.ac.kr
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221017T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>The a
 uthors:&nbsp\;<a href="https://harryjo97.github.io/">Jaehyeong Jo</a>&nbsp\
 ;who is a PhD student at the&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.mlai-kaist.com/">Ma
 chine Learning and Artificial Intelligence (MLAI) lab</a>&nbsp\;in KAIST\, 
 under the supervision of Prof.&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.sungjuhwang.com/">
 Sung Ju Hwang</a>. He received his B.S. (Mathematical Sciences) degree at K
 AIST in 2020.&nbsp\;<a href="https://seullee05.github.io/">Seul Lee</a>&nbs
 p\;who works in the same lab and&nbsp\;is interested in&nbsp\;deep drug dis
 covery\, generative models\, and graph representation learning.<br><br><b>P
 aper:</b><br><b>Score-based Generative Modeling of Graphs via the System of
  Stochastic Differential Equations&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs
 /2202.02514" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">https://arx
 iv.org/abs/2202.02514</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searc
 htype=author&query=Jo%2C+J"><u>Jaehyeong Jo</u></a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https:
 //arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Lee%2C+S">Seul Lee</a>\,&nbsp
 \;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Hwang%2C+S+J
 ">Sung Ju Hwang</a>)<br>Generating graph-structured data requires learning 
 the underlying distribution of graphs. Yet\, this is a challenging problem\
 , and the previous graph generative methods either fail to capture the perm
 utation-invariance property of graphs or cannot sufficiently model the comp
 lex dependency between nodes and edges\, which is crucial for generating re
 al-world graphs such as molecules. To overcome such limitations\, we propos
 e a novel score-based generative model for graphs with a continuous-time fr
 amework. Specifically\, we propose a new graph diffusion process that model
 s the joint distribution of the nodes and edges through a system of stochas
 tic differential equations (SDEs). Then\, we derive novel score matching ob
 jectives tailored for the proposed diffusion process to estimate the gradie
 nt of the joint log-density with respect to each component\, and introduce 
 a new solver for the system of SDEs to efficiently sample from the reverse 
 diffusion process. We validate our graph generation method on diverse datas
 ets\, on which it either achieves significantly superior or competitive per
 formance to the baselines. Further analysis shows that our method is able t
 o generate molecules that lie close to the training distribution yet do not
  violate the chemical valency rule\, demonstrating the effectiveness of the
  system of SDEs in modeling the node-edge relationships. Our code is availa
 ble at&nbsp\;<a href="https://github.com/harryjo97/GDSS">this https URL</a>
 .<br><b><br></b><u></u><br><u></u><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monda
 y at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</
 i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5
 pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a
 ><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href
 ="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4
 mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~B
 Qy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\,
  recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.
 com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></
 u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
