DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240219T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=TENTATIVE;CN=yuhki
 .mitsufuji@sony.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:yuhki.mitsufuji@sony.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ba
 c.nguyencong@sony.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bac.nguyencong@sony.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ch
 ieh-hsin.lai@sony.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:chieh-hsin.lai@sony.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240219T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Jesse (La
 i\, Chieh-hsin) and Yuki (Mitsufuji\, Yuhki)<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Con
 sistency Trajectory Models: Learning Probability Flow ODE Trajectory of Dif
 fusion </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.02279">https://arxiv.org/abs
 /2310.02279</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp
 \;query=Kim\,+D">Dongjun Kim</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?sea
 rchtype=author&amp\;query=Lai\,+C">Chieh-Hsin Lai</a>\, <a href="https://ar
 xiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Liao\,+W">Wei-Hsiang Liao</a
 >\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Murat
 a\,+N">Naoki Murata</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=a
 uthor&amp\;query=Takida\,+Y">Yuhta Takida</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/
 search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Uesaka\,+T">Toshimitsu Uesaka</a>\, 
 <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=He\,+Y">Y
 utong He</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;
 query=Mitsufuji\,+Y">Yuki Mitsufuji</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search
 /cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Ermon\,+S">Stefano Ermon</a>)<br>Consisten
 cy Models (CM) (Song et al.\, 2023) accelerate score-based diffusion model 
 sampling at the cost of sample quality but lack a natural way to trade-off 
 quality for speed. To address this limitation\, we propose Consistency Traj
 ectory Model (CTM)\, a generalization encompassing CM and score-based model
 s as special cases. CTM trains a single neural network that can -- in a sin
 gle forward pass -- output scores (i.e.\, gradients of log-density) and ena
 bles unrestricted traversal between any initial and final time along the Pr
 obability Flow Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE) in a diffusion process.
  CTM enables the efficient combination of adversarial training and denoisin
 g score matching loss to enhance performance and achieves new state-of-the-
 art FIDs for single-step diffusion model sampling on CIFAR-10 (FID 1.73) an
 d ImageNet at 64X64 resolution (FID 2.06). CTM also enables a new family of
  sampling schemes\, both deterministic and stochastic\, involving long jump
 s along the ODE solution trajectories. It consistently improves sample qual
 ity as computational budgets increase\, avoiding the degradation seen in CM
 . Furthermore\, CTM's access to the score accommodates all diffusion model 
 inference techniques\, including exact likelihood computation.<br><b><br></
 b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm
  UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?p
 wd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGT
 XlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion an
 d paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invit
 e/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/share
 d_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information:
  Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u>
 <a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark
 .com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u>
