ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20221003T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=cl
 ement.vignac@epfl.ch;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:clement.vignac@epfl.ch
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221031T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First
  author&nbsp\;<a href="https://cvignac.github.io/">Clément Vignac</a>&nbsp\
 ;who is a PhD student at EPFL in the lab of Prof. Pascal Frossard. He works
  on ML for sets and graphs\, incorporating symmetry priors of these data mo
 dalities\, and graph generation.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>DiGress: Discre
 te Denoising diffusion for graph generation&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://arxi
 v.org/abs/2209.14734" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">ht
 tps://arxiv.org/abs/2209.14734</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search
 /cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Vignac%2C+C" style="background-color: var(
 --textfield-surface)\; display: inline-block\;" class="paper-link">Clement 
 Vignac</a><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: 
 var(--on-surface)\;">\,</span><span style="background-color: var(--textfiel
 d-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">&nbsp\;</span><a href="https://arx
 iv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Krawczuk%2C+I" style="backgro
 und-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; display: inline-block\;" class="paper
 -link">Igor Krawczuk</a><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surf
 ace)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">\,</span><span style="background-color: 
 var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">&nbsp\;</span><a hre
 f="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Siraudin%2C+A" 
 style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; display: inline-block\;
 " class="paper-link">Antoine Siraudin</a><span style="background-color: var
 (--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">\,</span><span style="b
 ackground-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">&nb
 sp\;</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;quer
 y=Wang%2C+B" style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; display: i
 nline-block\;" class="paper-link">Bohan Wang</a><span style="background-col
 or: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">\,</span><span s
 tyle="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)
 \;">&nbsp\;</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&am
 p\;query=Cevher%2C+V" style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; d
 isplay: inline-block\;" class="paper-link">Volkan Cevher</a><span style="ba
 ckground-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">\,</
 span><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(-
 -on-surface)\;">&nbsp\;</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchty
 pe=author&amp\;query=Frossard%2C+P" style="background-color: var(--textfiel
 d-surface)\; display: inline-block\;" id="ow513" __is_owner="true" class="p
 aper-link">Pascal Frossard</a>) 2022<br>This work introduces DiGress\, a di
 screte denoising diffusion model for generating graphs with categorical nod
 e and edge attributes. Our model defines a diffusion process that progressi
 vely edits a graph with noise (adding or removing edges\, changing the cate
 gories)\, and a graph transformer network that learns to revert this proces
 s. With these two ingredients in place\, we reduce distribution learning ov
 er graphs to a simple sequence of classification tasks. We further improve 
 sample quality by proposing a new Markovian noise model that preserves the 
 marginal distribution of node and edge types during diffusion\, and by addi
 ng auxiliary graph-theoretic features derived from the noisy graph at each 
 diffusion step. Finally\, we propose a guidance procedure for conditioning 
 the generation on graph-level features. Overall\, DiGress achieves state-of
 -the-art performance on both molecular and non-molecular datasets\, with up
  to 3x validity improvement on a dataset of planar graphs. In particular\, 
 it is the first model that scales to the large GuacaMol dataset containing 
 1.3M drug-like molecules without using a molecule-specific representation s
 uch as SMILES or fragments.<b><br><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Eve
 ry Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4
 vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5
 pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b
 ><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~
 BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-
 ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming 
 papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hanne
 s-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-gro
 up</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
