ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=xi
 angfu@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:xiangfu@mit.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240205T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Xiang Fu<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>M
 OFDiff: Coarse-grained Diffusion for Metal-Organic Framework Design </b><a 
 href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.10732"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.10732
 </u></a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=author&query
 =Fu\,+X"><u>Xiang Fu</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/physics?se
 archtype=author&query=Xie\,+T"><u>Tian Xie</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv
 .org/search/physics?searchtype=author&query=Rosen\,+A+S"><u>Andrew S. Rosen
 </u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=author&quer
 y=Jaakkola\,+T"><u>Tommi Jaakkola</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/sear
 ch/physics?searchtype=author&query=Smith\,+J"><u>Jake Smith</u></a>)<br>Met
 al-organic frameworks (MOFs) are of immense interest in applications such a
 s gas storage and carbon capture due to their exceptional porosity and tuna
 ble chemistry. Their modular nature has enabled the use of template-based m
 ethods to generate hypothetical MOFs by combining molecular building blocks
  in accordance with known network topologies. However\, the ability of thes
 e methods to identify top-performing MOFs is often hindered by the limited 
 diversity of the resulting chemical space. In this work\, we propose MOFDif
 f: a coarse-grained (CG) diffusion model that generates CG MOF structures t
 hrough a denoising diffusion process over the coordinates and identities of
  the building blocks. The all-atom MOF structure is then determined through
  a novel assembly algorithm. Equivariant graph neural networks are used for
  the diffusion model to respect the permutational and roto-translational sy
 mmetries. We comprehensively evaluate our model's capability to generate va
 lid and novel MOF structures and its effectiveness in designing outstanding
  MOF materials for carbon capture applications with molecular simulations.<
 br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5
 pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/
 5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/57757225
 30?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for d
 iscussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/
 shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t
 /logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All 
 information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>
 :<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://
 hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u
 ><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
