DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="
 https://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=author&amp\;query=%C5%A0%C3%ADp
 ka%2C+M"><u>Martin Šípka</u></a>\, first author of the paper<br><br><b>Pape
 r:</b><br><b>Differentiable Simulations for Enhanced Sampling of Rare Event
 s </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.03480">https://arxiv.org/abs/2301
 .03480</a><b> (</b><a href="https://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=aut
 hor&amp\;query=%C5%A0%C3%ADpka%2C+M"><u>Martin Šípka</u></a>\, <a href="htt
 ps://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Dietschreit%2C+J
 +C+B">Johannes C. B. Dietschreit</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/ph
 ysics?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Grajciar%2C+L">Lukáš Grajciar</a>\, <a h
 ref="https://arxiv.org/search/physics?searchtype=author&amp\;query=G%C3%B3m
 ez-Bombarelli%2C+R">Rafael Gómez-Bombarelli</a>)<br>Simulating rare events\
 , such as the transformation of a reactant into a product in a chemical rea
 ction typically requires enhanced sampling techniques that rely on heuristi
 cally chosen collective variables (CVs). We propose using differentiable si
 mulations (DiffSim) for the discovery and enhanced sampling of chemical tra
 nsformations without a need to resort to preselected CVs\, using only a dis
 tance metric. Reaction path discovery and estimation of the biasing potenti
 al that enhances the sampling are merged into a single end-to-end problem t
 hat is solved by path-integral optimization. This is achieved by introducin
 g multiple improvements over standard DiffSim such as partial backpropagati
 on and graph mini-batching making DiffSim training stable and efficient. Th
 e potential of DiffSim is demonstrated in the successful discovery of trans
 ition paths for the Muller-Brown model potential as well as a benchmark che
 mical system - alanine dipeptide.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b>
 <i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.  
 </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRM
 m5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09<
 /a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a hr
 ef="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4
 B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj
 ~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers
 \, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-star
 k.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a>
 </u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
