UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=al
 exanderytong@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:alexanderytong@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=k.necl
 udov@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:k.necludov@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:vdujn2
 pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=l.
 atanackovic@mail.utoronto.ca;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:l.atanackovic@mail.utoro
 nto.ca
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20241021T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Lazar Ata
 nackovic who is a Ph.D. Candidate at the University of Toronto in The Depar
 tment of Electrical &amp\; Computer Engineering and the Vector Institute.<b
 r><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Meta Flow Matching: Integrating Vector Fields on 
 the Wasserstein Manifold </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.14608">htt
 ps://arxiv.org/abs/2408.14608</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?sea
 rchtype=author&amp\;query=Atanackovic\,+L">Lazar Atanackovic</a>\, <a href=
 "https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Zhang\,+X">Xi Zha
 ng</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=
 Amos\,+B">Brandon Amos</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtyp
 e=author&amp\;query=Blanchette\,+M">Mathieu Blanchette</a>\, <a href="https
 ://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Lee\,+L+J">Leo J. Lee</
 a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Beng
 io\,+Y">Yoshua Bengio</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype
 =author&amp\;query=Tong\,+A">Alexander Tong</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Neklyudov\,+K">Kirill Neklyudov</a
 >)<br>Numerous biological and physical processes can be modeled as systems 
 of interacting entities evolving continuously over time\, e.g. the dynamics
  of communicating cells or physical particles. Learning the dynamics of suc
 h systems is essential for predicting the temporal evolution of populations
  across novel samples and unseen environments. Flow-based models allow for 
 learning these dynamics at the population level - they model the evolution 
 of the entire distribution of samples. However\, current flow-based models 
 are limited to a single initial population and a set of predefined conditio
 ns which describe different dynamics. We argue that multiple processes in n
 atural sciences have to be represented as vector fields on the Wasserstein 
 manifold of probability densities. That is\, the change of the population a
 t any moment in time depends on the population itself due to the interactio
 ns between samples. In particular\, this is crucial for personalized medici
 ne where the development of diseases and their respective treatment respons
 e depends on the microenvironment of cells specific to each patient. We pro
 pose Meta Flow Matching (MFM)\, a practical approach to integrating along t
 hese vector fields on the Wasserstein manifold by amortizing the flow model
  over the initial populations. Namely\, we embed the population of samples 
 using a Graph Neural Network (GNN) and use these embeddings to train a Flow
  Matching model. This gives MFM the ability to generalize over the initial 
 distributions unlike previously proposed methods. We demonstrate the abilit
 y of MFM to improve prediction of individual treatment responses on a large
  scale multi-patient single-cell drug screen dataset.<br><b><br></b><b>Meet
 ing Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 C
 E(S)T  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU
 4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNT
 hhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and pap
 er voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-
 2nmy5vsj7-8KEDXe~mU~p5fCxwupSv5w" target="_blank">https://join.slack.com/t/
 logag/shared_invite/zt-2nmy5vsj7-8KEDXe~mU~p5fCxwupSv5w</a><br><br><b>All i
 nformation: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:
 <br></b><a href="https://portal.valencelabs.com/logg" target="_blank">https
 ://portal.valencelabs.com/logg</a><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u
 ></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T170220Z
