ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ww
 j@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:wwj@mit.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=xu
 minkai@mila.quebec;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:xuminkai@mila.quebec
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220524T170000
CREATED:20220820T195616Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the
  paper <a href="https://wwj.mit.edu/wujie-wangs-website" id="ow580" __is_ow
 ner="true">Wujie Wang</a>&nbsp\;who is a&nbsp\;4th year graduate student at
  MIT in Materials Sc. &amp\; Eng. He holds a B.A. in Physics from Wesleyan 
 and B.S in Engineering and Applied Sciences from Caltech. Also joining us i
 s <a href="https://minkaixu.com/" id="ow643" __is_owner="true">Minkai Xu</a
 >&nbsp\;who was working at MILA with Jian Tang and now received a Standford
  Graduate Fellowship with which he will pursue his PhD at Stanford.<br><br>
 <b>Paper:</b><br>Generative Coarse-Graining of Molecular Conformations&nbsp
 \;https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.12176 (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?se
 archtype=author&amp\;query=Wang%2C+W" class="paper-link" style="display: in
 line-block\;">Wujie Wang</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?s
 earchtype=author&amp\;query=Xu%2C+M" class="paper-link" style="display: inl
 ine-block\;">Minkai Xu</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?sea
 rchtype=author&amp\;query=Cai%2C+C" class="paper-link" style="display: inli
 ne-block\;">Chen Cai</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searc
 htype=author&amp\;query=Miller%2C+B+K" class="paper-link" style="display: i
 nline-block\;">Benjamin Kurt Miller</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/
 search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Smidt%2C+T" class="paper-link" style
 ="display: inline-block\;">Tess Smidt</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Wang%2C+Y" class="paper-link" styl
 e="display: inline-block\;">Yusu Wang</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Tang%2C+J" class="paper-link" styl
 e="display: inline-block\;">Jian Tang</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=G%C3%B3mez-Bombarelli%2C+R" id="ow
 576" __is_owner="true" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">R
 afael Gómez-Bombarelli</a>) 2022<br>Coarse-graining (CG) of molecular simul
 ations simplifies the particle representation by grouping selected atoms in
 to pseudo-beads and therefore drastically accelerates simulation. However\,
  such CG procedure induces information losses\, which makes accurate backma
 pping\, i.e.\, restoring fine-grained (FG) coordinates from CG coordinates\
 , a long-standing challenge. Inspired by the recent progress in generative 
 models and equivariant networks\, we propose a novel model that rigorously 
 embeds the vital probabilistic nature and geometric consistency requirement
 s of the backmapping transformation. Our model encodes the FG uncertainties
  into an invariant latent space and decodes them back to FG geometries via 
 equivariant convolutions. To standardize the evaluation of this domain\, we
  further provide three comprehensive benchmarks based on molecular dynamics
  trajectories. Extensive experiments show that our approach always recovers
  more realistic structures and outperforms existing data-driven methods wit
 h a significant margin.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every T
 uesday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2
 JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT
 09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a
  href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCX
 GjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>
 u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Sched
 ule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a hre
 f="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/l
 ogag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
