 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=gc
 orso@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:gcorso@mit.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=bjing@
 mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bjing@mit.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220607T170000
CREATED:20220820T195614Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First authors <a hr
 ef="https://gcorso.github.io/" id="ow567" __is_owner="true">Gabriele Corso<
 /a> and <a href="https://people.csail.mit.edu/bjing/" id="ow554" __is_owner
 ="true">Bowen Jing</a> who both are PhD students at MIT. Bowen is co-superv
 ised by Prof. Tommi Jaakkola and Prof. Bonnie Berger. Gabriele by Prof Jaak
 kola and Prof. Regina Barzilay.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br>Torsional Diffusion
  for Molecular Conformer Generation (arXiv coming soon) (<a href="https://o
 penreview.net/profile?id=~Bowen_Jing1" id="ow588" __is_owner="true"><i>Bowe
 n Jing</i></a><i>\,&nbsp\;</i><a href="https://openreview.net/profile?id=~G
 abriele_Corso1"><i>Gabriele Corso</i></a><i>\,&nbsp\;</i><a href="https://o
 penreview.net/profile?id=~Regina_Barzilay1"><i>Regina Barzilay</i></a><i>\,
 &nbsp\;</i><a href="https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Tommi_S._Jaakkola1" 
 id="ow584" __is_owner="true"><i>Tommi S. Jaakkola</i></a>) 2022<br>Diffusio
 n-based generative models generate samples by mapping noise to data via the
  reversal of a diffusion process that typically consists of independent Gau
 ssian noise in every data coordinate. This diffusion process is\, however\,
  not well suited to the fundamental task of molecular conformer generation 
 where the degrees of freedom differentiating conformers lie mostly in torsi
 on angles. We\, therefore\, propose Torsional Diffusion that generates conf
 ormers by leveraging the definition of a diffusion process over the space T
 ^m\, a high dimensional torus representing torsion angles\, and a SE(3)-equ
 ivariant model capable of accurately predicting the score over this process
 . Empirically\, we demonstrate that our model outperforms state-of-the-art 
 methods in terms of both diversity and precision of generated conformers\, 
 reducing the mean minimum RMSD by respectively 31% and 17%. When compared t
 o Gaussian diffusion models\, torsional diffusion enables significantly mor
 e accurate generation while performing two orders of magnitude fewer infere
 nce time-steps.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday a
 t</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><
 br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT
 09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><b
 r><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="h
 ttps://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSo
 kvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec
 -<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of u
 pcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https
 ://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-rea
 ding-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195616Z
