ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=al
 exander.tong@mila.quebec;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:alexander.tong@mila.quebec
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=jo
 ey.bose@mail.mcgill.ca;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:joey.bose@mail.mcgill.ca
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ta
 ra@dreamfold.ai;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:tara@dreamfold.ai
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20231218T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Joey Bose
  and hopefully also Alex Tong.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>SE(3)-Stochastic 
 Flow Matching for Protein Backbone Generation </b><a href="https://arxiv.or
 g/abs/2310.02391">https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.02391</a> (<a href="https://ar
 xiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bose\,+A+J">Avishek Joey Bos
 e</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=A
 khound-Sadegh\,+T">Tara Akhound-Sadegh</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/sea
 rch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Fatras\,+K">Kilian Fatras</a>\, <a href
 ="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Huguet\,+G">Guil
 laume Huguet</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&a
 mp\;query=Rector-Brooks\,+J">Jarrid Rector-Brooks</a>\, <a href="https://ar
 xiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Liu\,+C">Cheng-Hao Liu</a>\,
  <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Nica\,+A
 +C">Andrei Cristian Nica</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searcht
 ype=author&amp\;query=Korablyov\,+M">Maksym Korablyov</a>\, <a href="https:
 //arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bronstein\,+M">Michael B
 ronstein</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;
 query=Tong\,+A">Alexander Tong</a>)<br>The computational design of novel pr
 otein structures has the potential to impact numerous scientific discipline
 s greatly. Toward this goal\, we introduce FoldFlow a series of novel gener
 ative models of increasing modeling power based on the flow-matching paradi
 gm over 3D rigid motions -- i.e. the group SE(3) -- enabling accurate model
 ing of protein backbones. We first introduce FoldFlow-Base\, a simulation-f
 ree approach to learning deterministic continuous-time dynamics and matchin
 g invariant target distributions on SE(3). We next accelerate training by i
 ncorporating Riemannian optimal transport to create FoldFlow-OT\, leading t
 o the construction of both more simple and stable flows. Finally\, we desig
 n FoldFlow-SFM coupling both Riemannian OT and simulation-free training to 
 learn stochastic continuous-time dynamics over SE(3). Our family of FoldFlo
 w generative models offer several key advantages over previous approaches t
 o the generative modeling of proteins: they are more stable and faster to t
 rain than diffusion-based approaches\, and our models enjoy the ability to 
 map any invariant source distribution to any invariant target distribution 
 over SE(3). Empirically\, we validate our FoldFlow models on protein backbo
 ne generation of up to 300 amino acids leading to high-quality designable\,
  diverse\, and novel samples.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>E
 very Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PST.  </i><
 br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT
 09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><b
 r><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="h
 ttps://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8
 BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX31gc85y
 ZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, re
 cordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com
 /logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><
 b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250330T034527Z
