DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240226T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240226T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20231211T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=bj
 ing@mit.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bjing@mit.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=bjing.
 mit@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bjing.mit@gmail.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20240226T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Bowen Jin
 g\, PhD Student at MIT supervised by Tommi Jaakkola and Bonnie Berger.<br><
 br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>AlphaFold Meets Flow Matching for Generating Protein
  Ensembles </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.04845">https://arxiv.org
 /abs/2402.04845</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=aut
 hor&amp\;query=Jing\,+B">Bowen Jing</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search
 /q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Berger\,+B">Bonnie Berger</a>\, <a href
 ="https://arxiv.org/search/q-bio?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Jaakkola\,+T"
 >Tommi Jaakkola</a>)<br>The biological functions of proteins often depend o
 n dynamic structural ensembles. In this work\, we develop a flow-based gene
 rative modeling approach for learning and sampling the conformational lands
 capes of proteins. We repurpose highly accurate single-state predictors suc
 h as AlphaFold and ESMFold and fine-tune them under a custom flow matching 
 framework to obtain sequence-conditoned generative models of protein struct
 ure called AlphaFlow and ESMFlow. When trained and evaluated on the PDB\, o
 ur method provides a superior combination of precision and diversity compar
 ed to AlphaFold with MSA subsampling. When further trained on ensembles fro
 m all-atom MD\, our method accurately captures conformational flexibility\,
  positional distributions\, and higher-order ensemble observables for unsee
 n proteins. Moreover\, our method can diversify a static PDB structure with
  faster wall-clock convergence to certain equilibrium properties than repli
 cate MD trajectories\, demonstrating its potential as a proxy for expensive
  physics-based simulations. Code is available at <a href="https://github.co
 m/bjing2016/alphaflow">this https URL</a>.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details
 :<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CST / 4pm UTC / 11am EST / 8a
 m PST.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOd
 U4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRM
 m5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br><
 /b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7a-FHwX3
 1gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-22y7n3k7
 a-FHwX31gc85yZCa0uF8BU7w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcomin
 g papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://han
 nes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-g
 roup</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240904T130202Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
