DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220802T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220802T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:FEEAEC38-0494-443E-BE84-F231E30E5AF5
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=ga
 oni@in.tum.de;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:gaoni@in.tum.de
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220802T170000
CREATED:20220820T195616Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First author <a hre
 f="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=3GIKgWoAAAAJ&amp\;hl=en" id="o
 w664" __is_owner="true">Nicholas Gao</a>&nbsp\;who is a PhD student in the 
 group of Stephan Günnemann at TU Munich.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Ab-Init
 io Potential Energy Surfaces by Pairing GNNs with Neural Wave Functions<a h
 ref="goog_1588713271">&nbsp\;</a></b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.05
 064" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">https://arxiv.org/a
 bs/2110.05064</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=au
 thor&amp\;query=Gao%2C+N" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;
 ">Nicholas Gao</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=
 author&amp\;query=G%C3%BCnnemann%2C+S" class="paper-link" style="display: i
 nline-block\;">Stephan Günnemann</a>)<br>Solving the Schrödinger equation i
 s key to many quantum mechanical properties. However\, an analytical soluti
 on is only tractable for single-electron systems. Recently\, neural network
 s succeeded at modeling wave functions of many-electron systems. Together w
 ith the variational Monte-Carlo (VMC) framework\, this led to solutions on 
 par with the best known classical methods. Still\, these neural methods req
 uire tremendous amounts of computational resources as one has to train a se
 parate model for each molecular geometry. In this work\, we combine a Graph
  Neural Network (GNN) with a neural wave function to simultaneously solve t
 he Schrödinger equation for multiple geometries via VMC. This enables us to
  model continuous subsets of the potential energy surface with a single tra
 ining pass. Compared to existing state-of-the-art networks\, our Potential 
 Energy Surface Network PESNet speeds up training for multiple geometries by
  up to 40 times while matching or surpassing their accuracy. This may open 
 the path to accurate and orders of magnitude cheaper quantum mechanical cal
 culations.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at</i>
 <i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a
  href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">h
 ttps://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br
 ><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https:
 //join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">
 https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u><
 /u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcomi
 ng papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://ha
 nnes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-
 group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220820T195616Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learning on Graphs and Geometry Reading Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
