ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20221003T150000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=il
 yes.batatia@ens-paris-saclay.fr;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:ilyes.batatia@ens-par
 is-saclay.fr
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=dp
 k25@cam.ac.uk;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:dpk25@cam.ac.uk
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=gr
 egorsimm@microsoft.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:gregorsimm@microsoft.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20221003T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><a href="htt
 ps://scholar.google.com/citations?user=fTVuWFMAAAAJ&amp\;hl=fr" id="ow833" 
 __is_owner="true">Ilyes Batatia</a>&nbsp\;who is a research intern at the U
 niversity of Cambridge and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/d%C3%A1vid-
 p%C3%A9ter-kov%C3%A1cs-9b8465104/" id="ow852" __is_owner="true">Dávid Péter
  Kovács</a>&nbsp\;who is a PhD student there.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>MA
 CE: Higher Order Equivariant Message Passing Neural Networks for Fast and A
 ccurate Force Fields</b>&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.07697" c
 lass="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">https://arxiv.org/abs/220
 6.07697</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author
 &amp\;query=Batatia%2C+I" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;
 ">Ilyes Batatia</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchty
 pe=author&amp\;query=Kov%C3%A1cs%2C+D+P" class="paper-link" style="display:
  inline-block\;">Dávid Péter Kovács</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/
 search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Simm%2C+G+N+C" class="paper-link" 
 style="display: inline-block\;">Gregor N. C. Simm</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="http
 s://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Ortner%2C+C" class="
 paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Christoph Ortner</a>\,&nbsp\;<a
  href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Cs%C3%A1n
 yi%2C+G" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Gábor Csányi</a
 >)<br>Creating fast and accurate force fields is a long-standing challenge 
 in computational chemistry and materials science. Recently\, several equiva
 riant message passing neural networks (MPNNs) have been shown to outperform
  models built using other approaches in terms of accuracy. However\, most M
 PNNs suffer from high computational cost and poor scalability. We propose t
 hat these limitations arise because MPNNs only pass two-body messages leadi
 ng to a direct relationship between the number of layers and the expressivi
 ty of the network. In this work\, we introduce MACE\, a new equivariant MPN
 N model that uses higher body order messages. In particular\, we show that 
 using four-body messages reduces the required number of message passing ite
 rations to just \\emph{two}\, resulting in a fast and highly parallelizable
  model\, reaching or exceeding state-of-the-art accuracy on the rMD17\, 3BP
 A\, and AcAc benchmark tasks. We also demonstrate that using higher order m
 essages leads to an improved steepness of the learning curves.<b><br><br></
 b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CEST / 3p
 m UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j
 /5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722
 530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for 
 discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag
 /shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t
 /<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokv
 g</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\,
  mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-rea
 ding-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
