DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20241014T190000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:b1qril1ke5kft3h5gbg6tqm1ob@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=lxe@ta
 mu.edu;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:lxe@tamu.edu
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=uehara
 m1@gene.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:ueharam1@gene.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20241014T180000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First and
  last authors Xiner Li and Masatoshi Uehara. Xiner is a 4th year PhD studen
 t at Texas AM with Shuiwang Ji. Masatoshi is an incoming Professor at the U
 niversity of Wisconsin-Madison (joining 25 Fall).<br><b><br></b><br><b>Pape
 r:</b><br><b>Derivative-Free Guidance in Continuous and Discrete Diffusion 
 Models with Soft Value-Based Decoding </b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/24
 08.08252">https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.08252</a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/
 search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Li\,+X">Xiner Li</a>\, <a href="http
 s://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Zhao\,+Y">Yulai Zhao</
 a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Wang
 \,+C">Chenyu Wang</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=aut
 hor&amp\;query=Scalia\,+G">Gabriele Scalia</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Eraslan\,+G">Gokcen Eraslan</a>\, <
 a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Nair\,+S">
 Surag Nair</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp
 \;query=Biancalani\,+T">Tommaso Biancalani</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org
 /search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Regev\,+A">Aviv Regev</a>\, <a href
 ="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Levine\,+S">Serg
 ey Levine</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\
 ;query=Uehara\,+M">Masatoshi Uehara</a>)<br>Diffusion models excel at captu
 ring the natural design spaces of images\, molecules\, DNA\, RNA\, and prot
 ein sequences. However\, rather than merely generating designs that are nat
 ural\, we often aim to optimize downstream reward functions while preservin
 g the naturalness of these design spaces. Existing methods for achieving th
 is goal often require ``differentiable'' proxy models (\\textit{e.g.}\, cla
 ssifier guidance or DPS) or involve computationally expensive fine-tuning o
 f diffusion models (\\textit{e.g.}\, classifier-free guidance\, RL-based fi
 ne-tuning). In our work\, we propose a new method to address these challeng
 es. Our algorithm is an iterative sampling method that integrates soft valu
 e functions\, which looks ahead to how intermediate noisy states lead to hi
 gh rewards in the future\, into the standard inference procedure of pre-tra
 ined diffusion models. Notably\, our approach avoids fine-tuning generative
  models and eliminates the need to construct differentiable models. This en
 ables us to (1) directly utilize non-differentiable features/reward feedbac
 k\, commonly used in many scientific domains\, and (2) apply our method to 
 recent discrete diffusion models in a principled way. Finally\, we demonstr
 ate the effectiveness of our algorithm across several domains\, including i
 mage generation\, molecule generation\, and DNA/RNA sequence generation. Th
 e code is available at \\href{<a href="https://github.com/masa-ue/SVDD">thi
 s https URL</a>}{<a href="https://github.com/masa-ue/SVDD">this https URL</
 a>}.<br><b><br><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><
 i>:00 PT / 12:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/577
 5722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target="_blank">https://zoom.
 us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Wo
 rkspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack
 .com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2nmy5vsj7-8KEDXe~mU~p5fCxwupSv5w" target="_bl
 ank">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2nmy5vsj7-8KEDXe~mU~p5
 fCxwupSv5w</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, rec
 ordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><a href="https://portal.valencelabs.c
 om/logg" target="_blank">https://portal.valencelabs.com/logg</a><b><br></b>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T170220Z
