DESCRIPTION:<u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Yuanqi Du and Jiajun He<br><br><b>Pap
 er:</b><br><b>FEAT: Free energy Estimators with Adaptive Transport </b><a h
 ref="https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11516" target="_blank"><u>https://arxiv.org
 /abs/2504.11516</u></a> (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=
 author&query=He\,+J" target="_blank"><u><u>Jiajun He</u></u></a>\, <a href=
 "https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&query=Du\,+Y" target="_bla
 nk"><u>Yuanqi Du</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtyp
 e=author&query=Vargas\,+F" target="_blank"><u>Francisco Vargas</u></a>\, <a
  href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&query=Wang\,+Y" targ
 et="_blank"><u>Yuanqing Wang</u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/st
 at?searchtype=author&query=Gomes\,+C+P" target="_blank"><u>Carla P. Gomes</
 u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&query=Her
 n%C3%A1ndez-Lobato\,+J+M" target="_blank"><u>José Miguel Hernández-Lobato</
 u></a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&query=Van
 den-Eijnden\,+E" target="_blank"><u>Eric Vanden-Eijnden</u></a>)<br>We pres
 ent Free energy Estimators with Adaptive Transport (FEAT)\, a novel framewo
 rk for free energy estimation -- a critical challenge across scientific dom
 ains. FEAT leverages learned transports implemented via stochastic interpol
 ants and provides consistent\, minimum-variance estimators based on escorte
 d Jarzynski equality and controlled Crooks theorem\, alongside variational 
 upper and lower bounds on free energy differences. Unifying equilibrium and
  non-equilibrium methods under a single theoretical framework\, FEAT establ
 ishes a principled foundation for neural free energy calculations. Experime
 ntal validation on toy examples\, molecular simulations\, and quantum field
  theory demonstrates improvements over existing learning-based methods.<br>
 <b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at 9</i><i>:00 PT / 1
 2:00 ET /  18:00 CE(S)T  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=
 ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09" target="_blank">https://zoom.us/j/5775722
 530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for 
 discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag
 /shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyElg" target="_blank"><u>http
 s://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-2zuxi7gd1-rLUgxg6gnCkhO7WlRsyEl
 g</u></a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordin
 gs\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><a href="https://portal.valencelabs.com/lo
 gg" target="_blank">https://portal.valencelabs.com/logg</a><b><br></b><u></
 u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
