DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20230320T170000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:4om8dkr7eu2gvvk4o4mi4c9bjg_R20230102T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=wmjlyj
 emaine@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:wmjlyjemaine@gmail.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=mi
 njiw@amazon.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:minjiw@amazon.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20230320T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>Dr. Minji
 e Wang is a Senior Applied Scientist at Amazon AI Shanghai Lab\, where he l
 eads the research and development in the interdisciplinary area of machine 
 learning and systems. He received his Ph.D. from New York University and ha
 s since been dedicated to building deep learning systems with high usabilit
 y and performance\, as well as applying machine learning to optimize system
 s. Dr. Wang is also a passionate open-source enthusiast and has founded and
  contributed to several well-known open-source projects\, including Minerva
 \, Apache MXNet\, MinPy\, and Deep Graph Library (DGL). Notably\, NVIDIA re
 cognized Minerva as one of the "Modern AI Engines\," while AWS has adopted 
 Apache MXNet as their deep learning framework of choice. Furthermore\, DGL 
 has become one of the most popular frameworks for developing and applying G
 raph Neural Networks technology.<br><br><b>Paper: not really a paper!</b><b
 r><b>DGL 1.0: Empowering Graph Machine Learning for Everyone <br></b>The ra
 pid growth of new Graph Machine Learning technology such as Graph Neural Ne
 tworks (GNNs) has propelled the development of new open source tools. In th
 is talk\, we will introduce Deep Graph Library (DGL) 1.0\, a significant mi
 lestone of its 3+ year of development. DGL 1.0 provides a comprehensive and
  user-friendly support for both academic research on state-of-the-art model
 s and industrial demands for scaling GNNs to large\, real-world graphs. We 
 will highlight one of the key new features -- DGL Sparse\, a new sparse mat
 rix programming abstraction designed for trending Graph Machine Learning mo
 dels such as diffusion-based GNNs\, Hypergraph Neural Networks and Graph Tr
 ansformers. Lastly\, we will illustrate some of the research efforts by the
  team behind in terms of of GNN scalability and graph data pipeline.<br><b>
 <br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>4pm CET / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PD
 T.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN
 2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQ
 T09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><
 a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQ
 y~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty
 5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming pa
 pers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-
 stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group
 </a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250330T034746Z
