BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220315T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220315T180000
DTSTAMP:20260325T005103Z
ORGANIZER;CN=vdujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:vd
 ujn2pbpkhgr5f55cm39qbmu8@group.calendar.google.com
UID:1hfd2s2r4hmta9og6idelbrfic_R20220118T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=br
 andstetter@ml.jku.at;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:brandstetter@ml.jku.at
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220315T170000
CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the paper profess
 or <a href="https://www.jku.at/institut-fuer-machine-learning/ueber-uns/tea
 m/ass-prof-dr-johannes-brandstetter/" id="ow3686" __is_owner="true">Johanne
 s Brandstetter</a>&nbsp\;who holds his professorship at&nbsp\;JKU Linz\, wh
 ere he previously worked with Prof. Sepp Hochreiter. He is a guest research
 er at the University of Amsterdam in Prof. Max Wellings's group and started
  working with Microsoft's molecular ML group. He has a physics and data sci
 ence background and was one of the main researchers at CERN who made the fi
 rst direct  observation of the Higgs boson decayinginto pairs of fermions! 
 Next to his impressive work on physics-informed ML he also works on RL\, NL
 P\, Few-Shot Learning\, and Generative Modeling.</html-blob><br><html-blob>
 <br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Geometric and Physical Quantities Improve E(3) Equi
 variant Message Passing&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.02905
 ">https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.02905</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/se
 arch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Brandstetter%2C+J">Johannes Brandstett
 er</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;
 query=Hesselink%2C+R">Rob Hesselink</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/
 search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=van+der+Pol%2C+E">Elise van der Pol<
 /a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;que
 ry=Bekkers%2C+E+J">Erik J Bekkers</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/se
 arch/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Welling%2C+M">Max Welling</a>) ICLR 20
 22<br>Including covariant information\, such as position\, force\, velocity
  or spin is important in many tasks in computational physics and chemistry.
  We introduce Steerable E(3) Equivariant Graph Neural Networks (SEGNNs) tha
 t generalise equivariant graph networks\, such that node and edge attribute
 s are not restricted to invariant scalars\, but can contain covariant infor
 mation\, such as vectors or tensors. This model\, composed of steerable MLP
 s\, is able to incorporate geometric and physical information in both the m
 essage and update functions. Through the definition of steerable node attri
 butes\, the MLPs provide a new class of activation functions for general us
 e with steerable feature fields. We discuss ours and related work through t
 he lens of equivariant non-linear convolutions\, which further allows us to
  pin-point the successful components of SEGNNs: non-linear message aggregat
 ion improves upon classic linear (steerable) point convolutions\; steerable
  messages improve upon recent equivariant graph networks that send invarian
 t messages. We demonstrate the effectiveness of our method on several tasks
  in computational physics and chemistry and provide extensive ablation stud
 ies.<br><b><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at 5pm CET /
  4pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PT</i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?p
 wd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGT
 XlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discussion an
 d paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/shared_invit
 e/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.slack.com/t/<u></u>logag
 /shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg</a><br><br>
 <b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list
 </b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">h
 ttps://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250330T034547Z
