CREATED:20210724T162031Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b><br><br>A
 aron Lou is a second year PhD student advised by Professor Stefano Ermon. H
 e is interested in developing generative models for highly structured geome
 tric data. <br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Reflected Diffusion Models </b><a hr
 ef="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.04740">https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.04740</a> 
 (<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Lou%2C
 +A">Aaron Lou</a>\, <a href="https://arxiv.org/search/stat?searchtype=autho
 r&amp\;query=Ermon%2C+S">Stefano Ermon</a>)<br>Score-based diffusion models
  learn to reverse a stochastic differential equation that maps data to nois
 e. However\, for complex tasks\, numerical error can compound and result in
  highly unnatural samples. Previous work mitigates this drift with threshol
 ding\, which projects to the natural data domain (such as pixel space for i
 mages) after each diffusion step\, but this leads to a mismatch between the
  training and generative processes. To incorporate data constraints in a pr
 incipled manner\, we present Reflected Diffusion Models\, which instead rev
 erse a reflected stochastic differential equation evolving on the support o
 f the data. Our approach learns the perturbed score function through a gene
 ralized score matching loss and extends key components of standard diffusio
 n models including diffusion guidance\, likelihood-based training\, and ODE
  sampling. We also bridge the theoretical gap with thresholding: such schem
 es are just discretizations of reflected SDEs. On standard image benchmarks
 \, our method is competitive with or surpasses the state of the art and\, f
 or classifier-free guidance\, our approach enables fast exact sampling with
  ODEs and produces more faithful samples under high guidance weight.<br><b>
 <br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Monday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm CES
 T / 3pm UTC / 11am EDT / 8am PDT.  </i><br><a href="https://zoom.us/j/57757
 22530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j/5775722530?pw
 d=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Workspace for discus
 sion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com/t/logag/share
 d_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ">https://join.slack.com/t/loga
 g/shared_invite/zt-1hcqybjyd-ty5Pbj~BQy~W4B4mQQVxDQ</a><br><br><b>All infor
 mation: Schedule of upcoming papers\, recordings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br>
 </b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group">https://hanne
 s-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b><br></b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u>
