RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20220621T170000
CREATED:20220820T195614Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><b>Speaker:<br></b>First author of the
  paper <a href="https://konstantinrusch.com/" id="ow880" __is_owner="true">
 Konstantin Rusch</a>&nbsp\;who is an applied math PhD student at ETH Zurich
  supervised by&nbsp\;<a href="https://math.ethz.ch/sam/the-institute/people
 /siddhartha-mishra.html" id="ow893" __is_owner="true"><u>Siddhartha Mishra<
 /u></a>. His research is focused on physics-based ML for developing new met
 hods and tackling scientific problems.<br><br><b>Paper:</b><br><b>Graph-Cou
 pled Oscillator Networks&nbsp\;</b><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.0229
 6" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">https://arxiv.org/abs
 /2202.02296</a>&nbsp\;(<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=auth
 or&amp\;query=Rusch%2C+T+K" class="paper-link" style="display: inline-block
 \;">T. Konstantin Rusch</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?se
 archtype=author&amp\;query=Chamberlain%2C+B+P" class="paper-link" style="di
 splay: inline-block\;">Benjamin P. Chamberlain</a>\,&nbsp\;<a href="https:/
 /arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Rowbottom%2C+J" class="pa
 per-link" style="display: inline-block\;">James Rowbottom</a>\,&nbsp\;<a hr
 ef="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Mishra%2C+S" c
 lass="paper-link" style="display: inline-block\;">Siddhartha Mishra</a>\,&n
 bsp\;<a href="https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp\;query=Bron
 stein%2C+M+M" id="ow876" __is_owner="true" class="paper-link" style="displa
 y: inline-block\;">Michael M. Bronstein</a>)<br>We propose Graph-Coupled Os
 cillator Networks (GraphCON)\, a novel framework for deep learning on graph
 s. It is based on discretizations of a second-order system of ordinary diff
 erential equations (ODEs)\, which model a network of nonlinear forced and d
 amped oscillators\, coupled via the adjacency structure of the underlying g
 raph. The flexibility of our framework permits any basic GNN layer (e.g. co
 nvolutional or attentional) as the coupling function\, from which a multi-l
 ayer deep neural network is built up via the dynamics of the proposed ODEs.
  We relate the oversmoothing problem\, commonly encountered in GNNs\, to th
 e stability of steady states of the underlying ODE and show that zero-Diric
 hlet energy steady states are not stable for our proposed ODEs. This demons
 trates that the proposed framework mitigates the oversmoothing problem. Fin
 ally\, we show that our approach offers competitive performance with respec
 t to the state-of-the-art on a variety of graph-based learning tasks.<br><b
 ><br></b><b>Meeting Details:<br></b><i>Every Tuesday at</i><i> </i><i>5pm C
 EST / 3pm UTC / 11am EST / 8am PDT.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</i><br><a href="https://z
 oom.us/j/5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09">https://zoom.us/j
 /5775722530?pwd=ZzlGTXlDNThhUDZOdU4vN2JRMm5pQT09</a><br><br><b>Slack Worksp
 ace for discussion and paper voting:<br></b><a href="https://join.slack.com
 /t/logag/shared_invite/zt-u0mbo1ec-zElmvd1oSCXGjXvxLSokvg">https://join.sla
 ck.com/t/<u></u>logag/shared_invite/zt-<u></u>u0mbo1ec-<u></u>zElmvd1oSCXGj
 XvxLSokvg</a><br><br><b>All information: Schedule of upcoming papers\, reco
 rdings\, mailing list</b><b>:<br></b><u><a href="https://hannes-stark.com/l
 ogag-reading-group">https://hannes-stark.com/logag-reading-group</a></u><b>
 <br></b><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
